# walks over encoded code driven by instruction effects, such as the constant-time check
#
# the constant-time walk reads an encoded function through the set's decode
# dispatch and follows secrecy from the seeds the caller gives through
# registers and memory extents by each row's footprint, refusing a secret
# that reaches a control transfer, an address or an input a row's timing
# depends on (`masc.core.ct`). it reads under the context the function runs
# under, since that is what decides a conditional row: the selection and
# state the caller compiled for, as aarch64 code that sets dit in its
# prologue or an `__arm_streaming` function. a set whose timing is `none`
# refuses before any walk, and one whose timing is not guaranteed is walked
# as any other but asked no row's latency, and code it clears is answered
# unguaranteed (`ct.required`).
#
# secrecy is held per register row of the set's file and per memory extent.
# a row is secret when some bit of it may hold a secret, so every row sharing
# storage with a secret is: a seed or a write taints each row overlapping the
# register it names, as the file's rows state the relation
# (`register.overlapping`), and a read asks its own row alone. a tuple holds
# no storage of its own, so the walk keeps no secrecy for it and asks its
# members for it, as it reads a pair's operand through both halves. a write leaves
# a row it overwrites holding what it writes, as eax's write zeroing the rest
# of rax or w0's of x0, and adds its secret to a row it overlaps and leaves
# part of, as al's within rax or a lane's within its vector register, whose
# version of its value it moves either way.
# an extent is named by the register its address is formed from, the version
# of that register's value, an offset and a length, so two extents are known
# apart only when both are of one version of one register and do not
# overlap, and every other pair may alias.
#
# the walk follows the stack pointer, the register the canonical frame address
# of the architecture the context enters is stated from, as an offset from
# its value on entry, and every register as wide as it as the same: each holds
# a known offset from it or none. a row's relation (`effect.affine`) writing a
# register as wide from one of a known offset makes the written one's known,
# as sub sp, sp, #16, mov x29, sp or lea rbp, [rsp + 8], and so does the stack
# pointer's own change a row states (`effect.Stack`), as push and pop. every
# other write leaves the rows it reaches of no known offset, as an alloca's
# sub sp, sp, a0 or a write of esp within rsp, two paths joining with
# different offsets leave none, and a call leaves none anywhere but in the
# registers its model preserves, so the offsets a loop reaches are finite. an extent addressed through a register
# of a known offset is named off the stack pointer's value on entry, its
# offsets added, so a frame slot stays one extent however the prologue moves
# sp and fp, and an access provably clear of every secret one is not aliased.
# one through a register of no known offset falls back to its version.
# an extent addressed by a symbol is named off the symbol's address, so a
# global stays one extent wherever its address is formed. the walk reads the
# address a symbol forms from the sites the caller gives, the fixups its
# builder left in the code, never from a mnemonic: each site's fixup kind
# states the part of the address its field holds (`fixup.Part`), and its
# relocation kind whether it reaches the symbol through its got slot and
# whether a low part names the instruction of its high part. a register a
# row's relation forms from a site's operand holds that part, as auipc's
# pcrel_hi20, adrp's page or x86 lea's rip-relative address, a low part added
# to a register holding the matching high part completes the address, as
# addi's pcrel_lo12 naming the auipc or a load's :lo12:, wherever in the code
# the two are, a copy or an immediate added carries it, and a load of a got
# slot leaves the symbol's address. paths joining with different addresses
# leave none, and an address the sites do not place is placed as any other.
# the caller's symbol handles name objects known apart, and an offset off one
# stays within its object, as a compiler's code does.
# a secret stored where the address is not known, or anything secret at a
# call, whose callee the walk does not read, may be anywhere afterwards,
# but in the memory the call's model keeps.
# no store makes memory public again, since a store the walk cannot place
# exactly may miss the secret it would overwrite. a register's version is
# the offset of the instruction that last wrote it, or of the join that
# merged two, so the states a loop reaches are finite and the worklist over
# instruction starts reaches a fixed point.
#
# an access the walk places off no symbol and in no frame slot, as a load
# through a pointer parameter or one a typed stream pops the address of, may
# alias every extent held, so the producer may state what it reads instead,
# as its secrecy types state a pointer's pointee: an access seed, naming the
# instruction's offset and the access by its operand or by its position in
# the footprint. what such an access reads then holds a secret only when its
# seed says so, so the value a load writes or pushes, or the old value an
# atomic read-modify-write or compare-exchange returns, takes the seed's
# secrecy joined with the rest of what the instruction reads. a store through
# it follows the seed too: a secret stored where the seed states none is
# refused, worded `ct.STORED`, and one where it states a secret is placed as
# any other store. an access with no seed keeps the conservative rule, and
# one the walk places off a symbol or in the frame its extents.
#
# the producer may state a private frame extent, its own slot whose address
# never escapes, named off the stack pointer's value on entry as the walk
# names every frame slot, so it holds at every instruction however the
# prologue moves sp and fp. no pointer from outside the function reaches a
# fresh frame whose addresses never escaped, and no callee, which was never
# given them, reads or writes it, so no access the walk does not place in the
# frame aliases a private extent. a secret stored where the address is not
# known, a call's memory it does not keep, a secret at any address after a
# call, or an extent held off another register's version or a symbol leaves
# a private extent holding its own secrecy, a load the walk does not place
# reads none of it, where no access seed decides, and a call's join takes
# nothing from it. an access the walk places in the frame follows the extent
# rule, private or not. the obligation is the producer's: every access to a
# private slot is formed from the stack pointer by offsets the walk follows,
# and its address is never stored, passed to a call, returned or formed
# where the walk loses its offset. with no private extent stated the walk is
# as it is without the rule.
#
# secrecy leaves a value only where the caller declares it public, at a
# declassify point: an instruction offset, a side and a place, as the
# trap guard before a division makes its condition public. a point before an
# instruction makes the place public as that instruction reads it, so what
# the instruction decides and writes from it is public, and the state after
# it keeps the place's own secrecy unless the instruction writes it. a point
# after an instruction makes the place it writes hold no secret from there
# until it is written again, memory until a secret may be stored where it is.
# a point on a register row makes public with it the rows lying within it,
# and after a write the rows that write overwrites, as a point after a write
# of eax makes rax public, while a row holding more than it keeps its secret.
# a point is applied each time its instruction is walked, so one inside a
# loop holds on every pass to the fixed point, and one on a path into a join
# reaches the join only on that path, merged there with what the others hold.
# a point never changes a row's class. a point at an offset where no
# instruction the walk reaches starts, or naming a place its instruction does
# not read before it or write after it, is answered unread.
#
# a call is walked through the callee's model its caller states for the call
# site (`Call`), a trusted claim, and with none every register and every
# address is secret after it when anything is before it. the model's join is
# whether its argument registers, the memory it names read or any memory it
# does not keep may hold a secret. the registers it preserves keep what they
# held, the stack pointer what it held before the call instruction, as the
# callee's return undoes what the call pushes, the registers it writes take
# the join, and those it states neither are as with no model. with a secret
# join every byte it does not keep may hold one after it, globals included,
# and so does every extent it writes. a secret reaching the callee through an
# argument register or a read extent the model does not state it accepts, or
# through memory it does not keep and no accepted read holds, refuses the call,
# worded `ct.UNCHECKED`, so a callee not checked constant time accepts none.
# a confined model states its callee reads no memory but what its reads name,
# its own frame and what it writes before reading it, so its join takes
# nothing from memory it does not keep: a secret at any address or in a held
# extent it neither keeps nor names read neither joins nor refuses the call.
# its arguments and reads join and refuse as any model's, and a secret join
# still leaves a secret anywhere after it. the claim is the producer's, of
# the same proof as acceptance, a callee checked constant time, and the walk
# does not check it: a model whose callee is not so checked is never confined.
# a tail call, a modeled jump, ends its path, its target not followed as no
# call's is. a model at an offset where no call or tail call the walk reaches
# starts, or one naming a register the file has no row of, writing one it
# preserves or reading zero, preserving no stack pointer, or accepting what it
# does not name read, is answered unread.
#
# code of a typed stream passes its values on an operand stack and in the
# entries of its index spaces, as wasm's locals and globals, and nests its
# control in blocks a branch names by depth. the walk first reads such code
# once in its own order, as the stream's readers do, observing each
# instruction on the stream the context holds, which the caller has entered
# into the function the code is the body of. that read resolves through the
# stream's hooks how many values each type of each signature stands for under
# the labels open there, and matches each block's opening with its split and
# its close by the structure the effects state, so a branch to a block goes to
# its close, or a loop's to its start. secrecy is then held per value of the
# operand stack, the bottom first, and per index space entry, and follows the
# signatures and the footprints: a value an instruction pops at a depth its
# effect names is an address, a count of elements, a condition or what chooses
# a target, a branch carries the values its label's type names down to its
# block's height, a block's params pass into it as they are, an entry written
# through an operand takes what is written, and every value an instruction
# pushes takes whether anything it reads is secret. control joins only at one
# height of the stack. a call leaves what it pushes, every entry and every
# address secret when anything is, and a value pushed as the polymorphic stack
# ends the code control reaches there.

use std.types.bool.bool;
use std.types.bool.false;
use std.types.bool.true;
use std.types.error.err;
use std.types.option.opt;
use std.types.result.res;
use std.types.size.usize;
use std.types.string.str;

use A: std.allocator;
use std.collections.vector;

use mink_arch: mink.catalog.arch;
use mink.model.reloc;

use masc.codec.walk;
use masc.core.config;
use masc.core.ct;
use masc.core.dispatch;
use masc.core.effect;
use masc.core.field;
use masc.core.fixup;
use masc.core.footprint;
use masc.core.index;
use masc.core.operand;
use masc.core.quantity;
use masc.core.register;
use masc.core.requirement;
use masc.core.set;
use masc.core.state;
use masc.core.stream;

# a memory extent from a register's value or a symbol's address plus an offset
# ---
# base:   the register holding the address, register.NONE for one off a symbol or an absolute address
# symbol: the caller's handle of the symbol whose address it is off, as a site names it, operand.NO_SYMBOL for none. an
#         extent names a base or a symbol, never both
# offset: added to it
# length: the bytes it covers
pub rec Extent {
    base:   register.Id;
    symbol: u32;
    offset: i64;
    length: u64;
}

# the bytes of a global, off a symbol's address
# ---
# symbol: the caller's handle of the symbol, as a site names it, never operand.NO_SYMBOL
# offset: added to its address
# length: the bytes it covers, 0 for a length the caller does not know
pub rec Global {
    symbol: u32;
    offset: i64;
    length: u64;
}

# an entry of one of a typed stream's index spaces, as a wasm function's param is a local
# ---
# space: the set-local index space (`operand.Typed.space`)
# index: the entry's index in it
pub rec Entry {
    space: u16;
    index: u32;
}

# a frame slot: an extent off the value its base register holds where an instruction starts, as a spill slot off sp or
# fp once the prologue has moved them
# ---
# at:     where the instruction starts
# extent: the slot
pub rec Slot {
    at:     u64;
    extent: Extent;
}

# where a secret is when the code starts, or for a frame slot from where its instruction starts, or whether one is in
# what an access reads
# ---
# register: a register's value
# memory:   the bytes of an extent off a register's value on entry, or of an absolute address, never off a symbol
# entry:    the value of an index space entry of a typed stream
# frame:    the bytes of a frame slot, which hold a secret each time the walk reaches its instruction, before it runs
# symbol:   the bytes of a global, secret for the whole function: a load overlapping them reads a secret, and a store of a
#           public value never makes them public, as no store does
# access:   the secrecy of what one memory access of one instruction reads, which the walk takes in place of the extents
#           it holds when it does not place the access off a symbol or in the frame
# private:  a frame extent no access the walk does not place in the frame reaches, for the whole function, which states
#           no secret of its own
pub tag Seed: u8 {
    register: register.Id;
    memory:   Extent;
    entry:    Entry;
    frame:    Slot;
    symbol:   Global;
    access:   Access;
    private:  Private;
}

# the producer's statement that bytes of the function's own frame are private: its own slot whose address never
# escapes, so a pointer from outside the function, a callee or memory the walk does not place never reaches it. named
# off the stack pointer's value on entry, as the walk names every frame slot, so it holds at every instruction however
# the prologue moves sp and fp
# ---
# offset: added to the stack pointer's value on entry, as -24 for a slot 24 bytes below it
# length: the bytes it covers, never 0
pub rec Private {
    offset: i64;
    length: u64;
}

# which memory access of an instruction an access seed names
# ---
# operand: each access of the operand it is through, by the operand's position: a memory operand, or a register
#          operand an access's address is in, as a register machine's
# index:   the access by its position in the instruction's footprint (`footprint.Footprint.memory`), for one no operand
#          names, as a wasm load whose address it pops
pub tag Accessor: u8 {
    operand: u8;
    index:   u32;
}

# the producer's statement of what one memory access of an instruction reads, as its secrecy types state a load through
# a pointer. it holds each time the walk reaches its instruction, for an access the walk places off no symbol and in no
# frame slot, the extent rule standing for one it does
# ---
# at:     where the instruction starts
# access: the access
# secret: whether what it reads may hold a secret. what an atomic read-modify-write or compare-exchange returns is what
#         it reads. a store through it of a value that may hold a secret is refused when it is not, worded
#         `ct.STORED`
pub rec Access {
    at:     u64;
    access: Accessor;
    secret: bool;
}

# seeds as a pointer to the caller's rows and a count
pub rec Secrets {
    at:  *Seed;
    len: u32;
}

# what a declassify point makes public
# ---
# register: the value of a register row of the set's file, a row as footprints name it, so x86's zf and not rflags
# memory:   the bytes of an extent, of a known length, off the register an access of the instruction is formed from, or
#           off a symbol an access of it is placed by
# entry:    the value of an index space entry of a typed stream
# value:    a value of a typed stream's operand stack, by depth from its top, 0 the top
# frame:    the bytes of a frame slot off a register's value where the instruction starts, of a known length, which an
#           access of the instruction through any register holds whole once the walk places both
pub tag Place: u8 {
    register: register.Id;
    memory:   Extent;
    entry:    Entry;
    value:    u32;
    frame:    Extent;
}

# which side of its instruction a declassify point is on
# ---
# before: the instruction reads the place as public, which holds what it held after the instruction unless the
#         instruction writes it, as a branch reads a guard's condition
# after:  the instruction writes the place and it holds no secret from there until it is written again, as a compare
#         leaves its result, or a spill the slot it stores
pub tag Side: u8 {
    before;
    after;
}

# where a value becomes public: a declassify point, which removes the secret from one value at one place and never
# makes a row's timing independent of its inputs
# ---
# at:    where the instruction starts
# side:  which side of it
# place: what it makes public, a place the instruction reads for a point before it and writes for one after it
pub rec Declassify {
    at:    u64;
    side:  Side;
    place: Place;
}

# declassify points as a pointer to the caller's rows and a count, in any order, more than one at an offset allowed
pub rec Declassified {
    at:  *Declassify;
    len: u32;
}

# no declassify point
pub val NO_DECLASSIFIED: Declassified = Declassified{at: nil, len: 0};

# registers as a pointer to the caller's ids and a count
pub rec Registers {
    at:  *register.Id;
    len: u32;
}

# no register
pub val NO_REGISTERS: Registers = Registers{at: nil, len: 0};

# extents as a pointer to the caller's rows and a count, each off the value its base register holds where the call
# starts, as a frame slot off sp or fp, or off no register for an address
pub rec Extents {
    at:  *Extent;
    len: u32;
}

# no extent
pub val NO_EXTENTS: Extents = Extents{at: nil, len: 0};

# what the caller states of the callee of one call site, a trusted claim the walk reads in place of the callee it does
# not see. what it accepts a secret in is sound only of a callee checked constant time in those, or one the toolchain
# proves so, and the walk refuses the call when a secret reaches the callee through anything else. the join of a call
# is whether its arguments, the extents it reads and any memory it does not keep may hold a secret, which is what the
# callee may compute from. a callee that takes a secret buffer through a pointer but no secret length accepts the
# buffer's extent and not the length's register
# ---
# at:             where the call starts: a call, or a tail call, a jump whose target the walk does not follow, as it
#                 follows no call's, and after which the path ends
# accepted:       the argument registers the callee is checked to take a secret in, each one `arguments` names, none for
#                 a callee not checked
# accepted_reads: the extents of `reads` the callee is checked to take a secret in, each one `reads` names, none for a
#                 callee not checked
# preserved:      the registers holding after the call what they held once the call instruction ran, its link written,
#                 each with the rows lying within it. the stack pointer is one, holding what it held before the call
#                 instruction, as the callee's return undoes what the call pushes. a program counter's row, as x86's rip,
#                 holds what the call instruction left, the return point the walk goes on from
# arguments:      the registers the callee reads its arguments from
# reads:          the memory the callee may read that the model keeps, as a buffer in the caller's frame a pointer argument
#                 reaches. memory it does not keep is read whatever this names, unless `confined`
# confined:       whether the callee reads no memory but what `reads` names, its own frame and what it writes before
#                 reading it, so the join takes nothing from memory it does not keep. a claim of the same proof as
#                 acceptance, the callee checked constant time, which the producer states only with that proof and
#                 the walk does not check. a checked callee taking no secret accepts nothing and may still be confined
# written:        the registers the callee leaves its results in or clobbers, which take the join. a register stated neither
#                 preserved nor written is secret after the call when anything is before it, as with no model
# writes:         the memory the callee may write, which takes the join, the kept memory it writes included
# kept:           the memory the callee leaves as it was but where `writes` names. every other byte may be written with the
#                 join, globals included
pub rec Call {
    at:             u64;
    accepted:       Registers;
    accepted_reads: Extents;
    preserved:      Registers;
    arguments:      Registers;
    reads:          Extents;
    confined:       bool;
    written:        Registers;
    writes:         Extents;
    kept:           Extents;
}

# call models as a pointer to the caller's rows and a count, in any order, one at an offset
pub rec Calls {
    at:  *Call;
    len: u32;
}

# no call model, so every call leaves every register and every address secret when anything is
pub val NO_CALLS: Calls = Calls{at: nil, len: 0};

# a symbolic operand of the code the caller encoded, the fixup its builder left there, which the walk places a
# symbol's address by
# ---
# at:      where its instruction starts
# operand: the operand it fills
# fixup:   the set-local fixup kind
# symbol:  the caller's handle of its symbol. two handles name objects known apart, so a caller resolves a symbol an
#          equate or an alias names to the handle of what it names
# addend:  what the operand adds to the symbol, as `sym+8` states 8, before the builder measures it from where its
#          relocation does
# partner: for a kind whose relocation names a partner (`reloc.PARTNER`), where the instruction starts whose site's
#          address it takes, as risc-v's pcrel_lo12 names the label of its auipc. 0 for any other
pub rec Site {
    at:      u64;
    operand: u8;
    fixup:   operand.FixupKind;
    symbol:  u32;
    addend:  i64;
    partner: u64;
}

# sites as a pointer to the caller's rows and a count, in ascending order of offset
pub rec Sites {
    at:  *Site;
    len: u32;
}

# no site, so no address is placed by a symbol
pub val NO_SITES: Sites = Sites{at: nil, len: 0};

# encoded code of one function, the bytes the caller encoded. code of a typed stream is the instructions of the
# function's body, read under a context whose stream the caller has entered into that function
# ---
# set:   the instruction set it is encoded in
# data:  its bytes
# len:   how many
# sites: the fixups the builder left in it, NO_SITES for none
pub rec Code {
    set:   *set.Set;
    data:  *u8;
    len:   usize;
    sites: Sites;
}

# a secret the walk found where constant-time code may hold none
# ---
# offset:  where the instruction that refuses it starts
# refusal: the one refusal record, worded once
pub rec Finding {
    offset:  u64;
    refusal: ct.Refusal;
}

# code the walk could not follow
# ---
# message: why, as bytes no row decodes or a transfer to where no code is
# offset:  where
pub rec Unread {
    message: str;
    offset:  u64;
}

# what the walk finds of a function
# ---
# clear:        no secret reaches what it may not
# refused:      the first secret that does
# unread:       the code cannot be followed, so nothing is decided
# unguaranteed: no secret reaches a control transfer or an address, and the set cannot guarantee any instruction's
#               timing, so no row's latency was asked, which the caller warns of, worded `ct.UNGUARANTEED`, and never
#               refuses
pub tag Verdict: u8 {
    clear;
    refused: Finding;
    unread:  Unread;
    unguaranteed;
}

pub val UNDECODED:    str = "bytes no row decodes under the context";
pub val UNDECIDED:    str = "an instruction whose footprint its values and the configuration in force do not decide";
pub val NOWHERE:      str = "a transfer to where no code is";
pub val INDIRECT:     str = "a jump to a target a register holds, which the walk cannot follow";
pub val UNSEEDABLE:   str = "a seed names a register the set's file has no row of, an entry its stream does not hold, a frame slot at an offset where no instruction the walk reaches starts, an access at one past the code, memory or a slot off a symbol, a global of no symbol, or a private extent of no length or in code with no call frames";
pub val UNTYPED:      str = "a stack type of a signature the stream does not resolve to a count of values";
pub val UNBALANCED:   str = "a value popped past the bottom of the operand stack or its block's, a popped value named past what the instruction pops, or control joining at two heights of the stack";
pub val UNSTRUCTURED: str = "blocks the code does not close in order, a depth past every block open, or code past its body's block";
pub val CAUGHT:       str = "a block whose catches take control from any throw in it, which the walk does not follow";
pub val TIMED:        str = "code of a typed stream whose set classifies its rows' timing, which no class states over the values a row pops";
pub val MISPLACED:    str = "a declassify point at an offset where no instruction the walk reaches starts";
pub val UNTOUCHED:    str = "a declassify point naming a place the instruction at its offset does not read before it or write after it";
pub val UNCALLED:     str = "a call model at an offset where no call or tail call of machine code the walk reaches starts, or a second model at one";
pub val UNANCHORED:   str = "a call model whose preserved registers omit the stack pointer";
pub val UNWRITTEN:    str = "a call model naming a register the set's file has no row of, an extent off both a register and a symbol, or as written one reading zero or sharing storage with one it names preserved";
pub val UNACCEPTED:   str = "a call model accepting a secret in a register it names no argument, or in an extent it names no read";
pub val UNACCESSED:   str = "an access seed at an offset within an instruction, or naming a memory access the instruction at its offset does not make";
pub val UNSITED:      str = "a site out of ascending order, at one past the code, at an offset within an instruction, or naming an operand past its instruction's";

# the version of a register's value on entry
val ENTRY: u64 = 0;

# the register file of a set that names no register, as a typed stream's
val NO_FILE: register.File = register.File{
    quantities:     quantity.NO_QUANTITIES,
    bindings:       quantity.NO_BINDINGS,
    slot_count:     0,
    classes:        nil,
    class_count:    0,
    class_names:    index.NO_ENTRIES,
    registers:      nil,
    register_count: 0,
    aliases:        nil,
    alias_count:    0,
    names:          index.NO_ENTRIES,
    columns:        nil,
    column_count:   0,
    lying:          nil,
    lying_first:    nil,
    views:          nil,
};

# an extent that may hold a secret
# ---
# base:    the register row its address is formed from, the stack pointer's for one of a register of a known offset,
#          effect.NO_ROW for an address no register forms
# version: the version of that register's value, ENTRY for one of a register of a known offset
# symbol:  with base effect.NO_ROW, the symbol whose address it is off, operand.NO_SYMBOL for an address the walk does
#          not place
# slot:    whether it is off the address of the symbol's got slot rather than the symbol's
# offset:  added to it
# length:  the bytes it covers, 0 for a length the walk does not know
rec Held {
    base:    u32;
    version: u64;
    symbol:  u32;
    slot:    bool;
    offset:  i64;
    length:  u64;
}

# what a register row holds of a symbol's address, as the sites of the instructions writing it place it
# ---
# piece:     fixup.WHOLE for the address, fixup.HIGH for its high part a low part completes, fixup.NO_PIECE for none
# symbol:    the symbol
# offset:    added to its address
# slot:      whether it is of the symbol's got slot rather than the symbol
# partnered: for a high part, whether a low part completes it only by naming its instruction as its partner, as
#            risc-v's pcrel_hi20, else by naming the same symbol and offset, as aarch64's page
# site:      for a high part, where the instruction that formed it starts
rec Formed {
    piece:     fixup.Piece;
    symbol:    u32;
    offset:    i64;
    slot:      bool;
    partnered: bool;
    site:      u64;
}

val UNFORMED: Formed = Formed{piece: fixup.NO_PIECE, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, offset: 0, slot: false, partnered: false, site: 0};

# a register row given a symbol's address or a part of one by the instruction walked
rec Forming {
    row:    u32;
    formed: Formed;
}

# the value a register holds as an offset from the stack pointer's on entry
# ---
# known:  whether the walk knows it
# offset: the offset, when it does
rec Frame {
    known:  bool;
    offset: i64;
}

val UNKNOWN: Frame = Frame{known: false, offset: 0};

# an extent the walk does not place
val UNPLACED: Held = Held{base: effect.NO_ROW, version: ENTRY, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: 0, length: 0};

# a register given a known offset by the instruction walked
# ---
# row:    its row
# offset: its offset from the stack pointer's value on entry
rec Moved {
    row:    u32;
    offset: i64;
}

# a register the instruction walked writes as a stated function of what it reads, so its secrecy is its inputs' and
# not all the instruction reads
# ---
# row:    its row
# secret: whether any input of its value may hold a secret
rec Derived {
    row:    u32;
    secret: bool;
}

# a register row as it was where a call starts
# ---
# row:     its row
# taint:   whether it may hold a secret
# version: its version
# frame:   its offset from the stack pointer's value on entry
rec Saved {
    row:     u32;
    taint:   bool;
    version: u64;
    frame:   Frame;
}

# what is secret where an instruction starts
# ---
# taint:    the register rows that may hold a secret in some bit, one bit per row, every row overlapping one that does
#           included
# versions: the version of each register row's value
# frames:   the offset of each register row's value from the stack pointer's on entry
# formed:   what each register row's value holds of a symbol's address
# held:     the extents that may hold a secret
# public:   the extents a declassify point after an instruction made public, which hold no secret whatever `held` and
#           `anywhere` say until a secret may be stored there
# anywhere: whether a secret may be at any address but those `spared` holds
# spared:   the extents a call model kept, which hold what `held` and `public` say even when `anywhere` is set, empty
#           unless it is
# config:   the configuration state in force, none when not known
# stack:    a typed stream's operand stack, the bottom first, whether each value may hold a secret
# entries:  the keys of the index space entries that may hold a secret, by `key`, ascending, or with `except` the
#           entries known to hold none
# except:   whether every entry `entries` does not name may hold a secret, as after a call
rec Point {
    taint:    vector.Vector[u64];
    versions: vector.Vector[u64];
    frames:   vector.Vector[Frame];
    formed:   vector.Vector[Formed];
    held:     vector.Vector[Held];
    public:   vector.Vector[Held];
    anywhere: bool;
    spared:   vector.Vector[Held];
    config:   opt[config.State];
    stack:    vector.Vector[bool];
    entries:  vector.Vector[u64];
    except:   bool;
}

# a memory access of one instruction, placed as the walk names extents
# ---
# reads:   whether it reads
# writes:  whether it writes
# operand: the memory operand whose access it is, field.NO_OPERAND for one an effect states through a pointer or none
# at:      the extent it touches
# row:     the register row its address is formed from, effect.NO_ROW for none
# rebased: what naming it off the stack pointer added to its offset from that row's value, 0 when it is not
# named:   the operand an access seed names it by: the one its footprint states it through, or its memory operand,
#          field.NO_OPERAND for none
# index:   its position in the footprint's accesses, NO_ACCESS for a memory operand the footprint states none of
# seeded:  whether an access seed states what it reads, which the walk takes for one it does not place
# secret:  with `seeded`, whether what it reads may hold a secret
rec Touch {
    reads:   bool;
    writes:  bool;
    operand: u8;
    at:      Held;
    row:     u32;
    rebased: i64;
    named:   u8;
    index:   u32;
    seeded:  bool;
    secret:  bool;
}

# what the walk's ordered read of a typed stream found of the instruction starting at one offset
# ---
# len:     its bytes
# counts:  where in `Walk.counts` the counts of its signature's types start, its pops' then its pushes', each how many
#          values the type stands for, 0 for the polymorphic stack
# targets: where in `Walk.targets` the blocks its depths name start
# depths:  how many
# block:   the block it opens, splits or closes, NO_BLOCK for none
# stuck:   whether it pushes the polymorphic stack, so control does not go on past it
rec Shape {
    len:     usize;
    counts:  u32;
    targets: u32;
    depths:  u32;
    block:   u32;
    stuck:   bool;
}

# a structured block of a typed stream's code
# ---
# open:    where the instruction opening it starts, NO_OFFSET for the function's body
# body:    where its first instruction starts
# split:   where the instruction splitting it into two arms starts, NO_OFFSET for none
# close:   where the instruction closing it starts, NO_OFFSET while it is open
# base:    the height of the operand stack below its params
# params:  how many values pass into it
# results: how many values it leaves
# loops:   whether its label is its start, else its close
rec Block {
    open:    usize;
    body:    usize;
    split:   usize;
    close:   usize;
    base:    u32;
    params:  u32;
    results: u32;
    loops:   bool;
}

# the walk's storage
# ---
# code:     the code walked
# timed:    whether each row's latency is asked, false for a set whose timing is not guaranteed
# ctx:      the context it runs under
# file:     the set's register file, NO_FILE for a set that names no register
# words:    the words a set over the file's rows spans
# stream:   the set's typed stream hooks, nil for a machine set
# points:   the state at each instruction start reached, by index into `states`, NO_POINT for none
# states:   the states
# work:     the instruction starts whose state changed and are not walked since
# named:    the rows the operands of the instruction walked name, one bit per row
# touches:  the memory accesses of the instruction walked
# shaped:   what the ordered read found of each instruction start of a typed stream, by index into `shapes`, NO_POINT
#           for none
# shapes:   what it found
# counts:   the counts of the shapes' signatures
# targets:  the blocks the shapes' depths name, by index into `blocks`
# blocks:   the blocks of a typed stream's code, the function's body first
# carried:  the values a branch of the instruction walked carries to its label, the deepest first
# popped:   the values the instruction walked pops, the deepest first
# public:   the caller's declassify points
# declared: the first declassify point at each offset, by index into `public`, NO_POINT for none
# chain:    the next declassify point at the offset of each, NO_POINT for none
# overlaps: the rows each row of the file shares storage with
# stack:    the stack pointer's row, effect.NO_ROW for a set whose code has no call frames
# moved:    the registers the instruction walked gives a known offset
# derived:  the registers it writes as a stated function of what it reads, with their inputs' secrecy
# secrets:  the caller's seeds
# sown:     the first frame seed at each offset, by index into `secrets`, NO_POINT for none
# sowing:   the next seed of its kind, frame or access, at the offset of each seed, NO_POINT for none
# stated:   the first access seed at each offset, by index into `secrets`, NO_POINT for none
# private:  the private extents the seeds state, off the stack pointer's value on entry
# calls:    the caller's call models
# called:   the call model at each offset, by index into `calls`, NO_POINT for none
# keeping:  the rows the call model of the instruction walked preserves, one bit per row
# writing:  the rows it writes, one bit per row
# kept:     the extents it keeps, placed where the call starts
# wrote:    the extents it writes, placed there
# saved:    the stack pointer's rows as they were where the call starts
# arch:     the architecture the context enters, whose bindings a site's relocation kind is read under, nil for none
# sited:    the first site at each offset, by index into `code.sites`, NO_POINT for none
# forming:  the registers the instruction walked gives a symbol's address or a part of one
# at:       where the instruction walked starts
rec Walk {
    a:        *A.Allocator;
    code:     *Code;
    timed:    bool;
    ctx:      *state.Context;
    file:     *register.File;
    words:    usize;
    stream:   *stream.Hooks;
    points:   vector.Vector[u32];
    states:   vector.Vector[Point];
    work:     vector.Vector[usize];
    named:    vector.Vector[u64];
    touches:  vector.Vector[Touch];
    shaped:   vector.Vector[u32];
    shapes:   vector.Vector[Shape];
    counts:   vector.Vector[u32];
    targets:  vector.Vector[u32];
    blocks:   vector.Vector[Block];
    carried:  vector.Vector[bool];
    popped:   vector.Vector[bool];
    public:   *Declassified;
    declared: vector.Vector[u32];
    chain:    vector.Vector[u32];
    overlaps: register.Overlaps;
    stack:    u32;
    moved:    vector.Vector[Moved];
    derived:  vector.Vector[Derived];
    secrets:  *Secrets;
    sown:     vector.Vector[u32];
    sowing:   vector.Vector[u32];
    stated:   vector.Vector[u32];
    private:  vector.Vector[Held];
    calls:    *Calls;
    called:   vector.Vector[u32];
    keeping:  vector.Vector[u64];
    writing:  vector.Vector[u64];
    kept:     vector.Vector[Held];
    wrote:    vector.Vector[Held];
    saved:    vector.Vector[Saved];
    arch:     *mink_arch.Arch;
    sited:    vector.Vector[u32];
    forming:  vector.Vector[Forming];
    at:       usize;
}

val NO_POINT:  u32   = 0xFFFF_FFFF;
val NO_BLOCK:  u32   = 0xFFFF_FFFF;
val NO_OFFSET: usize = 0xFFFF_FFFF_FFFF_FFFF;
val NO_ACCESS: u32   = 0xFFFF_FFFF;

fun bit_of(words: *u64, row: u32) bool {
    ret (words[row / 64] & (1::u64 << (row % 64)::u64)) != 0;
}

fun set_bit(words: *u64, row: u32, on: bool) {
    val mask: u64 = 1::u64 << (row % 64)::u64;
    if (on) { words[row / 64] = words[row / 64] | mask; }
    or      { words[row / 64] = words[row / 64] & ~mask; }
}

fun failed[T](e: A.Error) res[T, A.Error] {
    ret res[T, A.Error].err{e};
}

# the key of entry `index` of space `space`, in the order the keys of a point's entries keep
fun key(space: u16, index: u32) u64 {
    ret (space::u64 << 32) | index::u64;
}

# where `k` is in the ascending `keys`, or where it would go
# ---
# held: whether it is there
# at:   its position, or the position it would take
rec Found {
    held: bool;
    at:   usize;
}

fun find_key(keys: *vector.Vector[u64], k: u64) Found {
    var lo: usize = 0;
    var hi: usize = keys.len;
    for (lo < hi) {
        val mid: usize = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
        if (keys.data[mid] < k) { lo = mid + 1; }
        or                      { hi = mid; }
    }
    ret Found{held: lo < keys.len && keys.data[lo] == k, at: lo};
}

# `k` added to the ascending `keys` unless they hold it
fun insert_key(keys: *vector.Vector[u64], k: u64) err[A.Error] {
    val f: Found = find_key(keys, k);
    if (f.held) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
    val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](keys, k);
    if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
    var i: usize = keys.len - 1;
    for (i > f.at) {
        keys.data[i] = keys.data[i - 1];
        i            = i - 1;
    }
    keys.data[f.at] = k;
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# `k` taken out of the ascending `keys` when they hold it
fun remove_key(keys: *vector.Vector[u64], k: u64) {
    val f: Found = find_key(keys, k);
    if (!f.held) { ret; }
    var i: usize = f.at;
    for (i + 1 < keys.len) {
        keys.data[i] = keys.data[i + 1];
        i            = i + 1;
    }
    vector.truncate[u64](keys, keys.len - 1);
}

# whether entry `k` may hold a secret under `p`
fun entry_secret(p: *Point, k: u64) bool {
    ret find_key(?p.entries, k).held != p.except;
}

# entry `k` made to hold a secret under `p` or none
fun set_entry(p: *Point, k: u64, secret: bool) err[A.Error] {
    if (secret != p.except) { ret insert_key(?p.entries, k); }
    remove_key(?p.entries, k);
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# whether some entry may hold a secret under `p`
fun any_entry(p: *Point) bool {
    ret p.except || p.entries.len > 0;
}

# a point of `w`'s file holding nothing secret, every register at its entry version and the operand stack empty
fun blank(w: *Walk) res[Point, A.Error] {
    var p: Point = Point{
        taint:    vector.init[u64](w.a),
        versions: vector.init[u64](w.a),
        frames:   vector.init[Frame](w.a),
        formed:   vector.init[Formed](w.a),
        held:     vector.init[Held](w.a),
        public:   vector.init[Held](w.a),
        anywhere: false,
        spared:   vector.init[Held](w.a),
        config:   opt[config.State].none{},
        stack:    vector.init[bool](w.a),
        entries:  vector.init[u64](w.a),
        except:   false,
    };
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < w.words) {
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](?p.taint, 0);
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[Point](pushed.err); }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < w.file.register_count::usize) {
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](?p.versions, ENTRY);
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[Point](pushed.err); }
        var f: Frame = UNKNOWN;
        if (i == w.stack::usize) { f = Frame{known: true, offset: 0}; }
        val framed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Frame](?p.frames, f);
        if (sel framed.err) { ret failed[Point](framed.err); }
        val formed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Formed](?p.formed, UNFORMED);
        if (sel formed.err) { ret failed[Point](formed.err); }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[Point, A.Error].ok{p};
}

fun drop(p: *Point) {
    vector.dnit[u64](?p.taint);
    vector.dnit[u64](?p.versions);
    vector.dnit[Frame](?p.frames);
    vector.dnit[Formed](?p.formed);
    vector.dnit[Held](?p.held);
    vector.dnit[Held](?p.public);
    vector.dnit[Held](?p.spared);
    vector.dnit[bool](?p.stack);
    vector.dnit[u64](?p.entries);
}

# a copy of `from`
fun copy(w: *Walk, from: *Point) res[Point, A.Error] {
    val made: res[Point, A.Error] = blank(w);
    if (sel made.err) { ret made; }
    var p: Point = made.ok;
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < w.words) {
        p.taint.data[i] = from.taint.data[i];
        i               = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < p.versions.len) {
        p.versions.data[i] = from.versions.data[i];
        p.frames.data[i]   = from.frames.data[i];
        p.formed.data[i]   = from.formed.data[i];
        i                  = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < from.held.len) {
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?p.held, from.held.data[i]);
        if (sel pushed.err) {
            drop(?p);
            ret failed[Point](pushed.err);
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < from.public.len) {
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?p.public, from.public.data[i]);
        if (sel pushed.err) {
            drop(?p);
            ret failed[Point](pushed.err);
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < from.spared.len) {
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?p.spared, from.spared.data[i]);
        if (sel pushed.err) {
            drop(?p);
            ret failed[Point](pushed.err);
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < from.stack.len) {
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[bool](?p.stack, from.stack.data[i]);
        if (sel pushed.err) {
            drop(?p);
            ret failed[Point](pushed.err);
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < from.entries.len) {
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](?p.entries, from.entries.data[i]);
        if (sel pushed.err) {
            drop(?p);
            ret failed[Point](pushed.err);
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    p.anywhere = from.anywhere;
    p.config   = from.config;
    p.except   = from.except;
    ret res[Point, A.Error].ok{p};
}

fun same(x: *Held, y: *Held) bool {
    ret x.base == y.base && x.version == y.version && x.symbol == y.symbol && x.slot == y.slot && x.offset == y.offset && x.length == y.length;
}

# whether `h` is off a symbol's address
fun symbolic(h: *Held) bool {
    ret h.base == effect.NO_ROW && h.symbol != operand.NO_SYMBOL;
}

# whether the walk places `h`: off a register's value or a symbol's address
fun located(h: *Held) bool {
    ret h.base != effect.NO_ROW || h.symbol != operand.NO_SYMBOL;
}

# `h` added to what `p` holds unless it holds it
fun hold(p: *Point, h: Held) err[A.Error] {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < p.held.len) {
        if (same(?p.held.data[i], ?h)) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?p.held, h);
    if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# whether `held` and `at` may share a byte: only extents of one version of one register, or off one symbol, both of
# known length, are known apart, when they do not overlap, and extents off two symbols or a symbol and its got slot
# always are
fun may_alias(held: *Held, at: *Held) bool {
    if (symbolic(held) && symbolic(at)) {
        if (held.symbol != at.symbol || held.slot != at.slot) { ret false; }
        if (held.length == 0 || at.length == 0)               { ret true; }
        ret held.offset < at.offset + at.length::i64 && at.offset < held.offset + held.length::i64;
    }
    if (held.base != at.base || held.version != at.version || held.base == effect.NO_ROW) { ret true; }
    if (held.length == 0 || at.length == 0)                                               { ret true; }
    ret held.offset < at.offset + at.length::i64 && at.offset < held.offset + held.length::i64;
}

# whether every byte of `inner` is one of `outer`: both of one version of one register, or off one symbol, and of known
# length
fun inside(inner: *Held, outer: *Held) bool {
    if (symbolic(inner) || symbolic(outer)) {
        if (!symbolic(inner) || !symbolic(outer) || inner.symbol != outer.symbol || inner.slot != outer.slot) { ret false; }
        if (inner.length == 0 || outer.length == 0)                                                           { ret false; }
        ret inner.offset >= outer.offset && inner.offset + inner.length::i64 <= outer.offset + outer.length::i64;
    }
    if (inner.base != outer.base || inner.version != outer.version || inner.base == effect.NO_ROW) { ret false; }
    if (inner.length == 0 || outer.length == 0)                                                    { ret false; }
    ret inner.offset >= outer.offset && inner.offset + inner.length::i64 <= outer.offset + outer.length::i64;
}

# the extents `p` knows public taken out where a secret stored at `at` may reach them, every one for an address the walk
# does not place but a private one
fun unpublish(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: *Held) {
    var kept: usize = 0;
    var i:    usize = 0;
    for (i < p.public.len) {
        if ((located(at) && !may_alias(?p.public.data[i], at)) || privately_apart(w, ?p.public.data[i], at)) {
            p.public.data[kept] = p.public.data[i];
            kept                = kept + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    vector.truncate[Held](?p.public, kept);
}

# whether every byte of `at` is one of an extent a call model kept under `p`
fun is_spared(p: *Point, at: *Held) bool {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < p.spared.len) {
        if (inside(at, ?p.spared.data[i])) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether every byte of `at` is one of a private extent of `w`, so no access the walk does not place in the frame
# reaches it
fun is_private(w: *Walk, at: *Held) bool {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < w.private.len) {
        if (inside(at, ?w.private.data[i])) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether the walk places `h` in the frame, off the stack pointer's value on entry
fun framed(w: *Walk, h: *Held) bool {
    ret w.stack != effect.NO_ROW && h.base == w.stack && h.version == ENTRY;
}

# whether `x` and `y` are known apart by a private extent: one lies within one and the walk does not place the other
# in the frame, so whatever else may alias the two may not
fun privately_apart(w: *Walk, x: *Held, y: *Held) bool {
    if (w.private.len == 0) { ret false; }
    ret (is_private(w, x) && !framed(w, y)) || (is_private(w, y) && !framed(w, x));
}

# whether memory under `p` may hold a secret a callee may read: at any address, or in a held extent that is not private
fun memory_secret(w: *Walk, p: *Point) bool {
    if (p.anywhere) { ret true; }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < p.held.len) {
        if (!is_private(w, ?p.held.data[i])) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# the extents `p` knows public kept only where they are private, as a secret made possible at every address the walk
# does not place in the frame leaves them
fun keep_private(w: *Walk, p: *Point) {
    var kept: usize = 0;
    var i:    usize = 0;
    for (i < p.public.len) {
        if (is_private(w, ?p.public.data[i])) {
            p.public.data[kept] = p.public.data[i];
            kept                = kept + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    vector.truncate[Held](?p.public, kept);
}

# a secret made possible at any address in `p`, none spared
fun everywhere(p: *Point) {
    p.anywhere = true;
    vector.truncate[Held](?p.spared, 0);
}

# the extents `spared` holds narrowed to the bytes `by` holds as well: each of either lying within one of the other,
# so what both spare and no more
# ---
# ret: whether `spared` changed
fun narrow(w: *Walk, spared: *vector.Vector[Held], by: *vector.Vector[Held]) res[bool, A.Error] {
    var kept: vector.Vector[Held] = vector.init[Held](w.a);
    var i:    usize               = 0;
    for (i < spared.len) {
        var k: usize = 0;
        for (k < by.len) {
            if (inside(?spared.data[i], ?by.data[k])) {
                val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?kept, spared.data[i]);
                if (sel pushed.err) {
                    vector.dnit[Held](?kept);
                    ret failed[bool](pushed.err);
                }
                k = by.len;
            }
            or { k = k + 1; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < by.len) {
        var within: bool  = false;
        var held:   bool  = false;
        var k:      usize = 0;
        for (k < spared.len) {
            if (inside(?by.data[i], ?spared.data[k])) { within = true; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        k = 0;
        for (k < kept.len) {
            if (same(?by.data[i], ?kept.data[k])) { held = true; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        if (within && !held) {
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?kept, by.data[i]);
            if (sel pushed.err) {
                vector.dnit[Held](?kept);
                ret failed[bool](pushed.err);
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    var changed: bool = kept.len != spared.len;
    i = 0;
    for (i < kept.len && !changed) {
        var k:     usize = 0;
        var found: bool  = false;
        for (k < spared.len) {
            if (same(?kept.data[i], ?spared.data[k])) { found = true; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        if (!found) { changed = true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    vector.dnit[Held](spared);
    @spared = kept;
    ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{changed};
}

# whether the bytes of `at` may hold a secret under `p`. a private extent holds none a secret at any address puts there,
# and an extent the walk does not place in the frame none a private one holds
fun secret_at(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: *Held) bool {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < p.public.len) {
        if (inside(at, ?p.public.data[i])) { ret false; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    if (p.anywhere && !is_spared(p, at) && !is_private(w, at)) { ret true; }
    i = 0;
    for (i < p.held.len) {
        if (may_alias(?p.held.data[i], at) && !privately_apart(w, ?p.held.data[i], at)) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# the entries of `from` merged into `into`'s, so the entries either may hold a secret in may in the join
# ---
# ret: whether `into`'s changed
fun merge_entries(w: *Walk, into: *Point, from: *Point) res[bool, A.Error] {
    var changed: bool  = false;
    var i:       usize = 0;
    if (!from.except) {
        # what from holds secret is secret in the join: added to into's secrets, or taken from what into knows public
        for (i < from.entries.len) {
            val k:      u64  = from.entries.data[i];
            val before: bool = entry_secret(into, k);
            if (!before) {
                val set: err[A.Error] = set_entry(into, k, true);
                if (sel set.err) { ret failed[bool](set.err); }
                changed = true;
            }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{changed};
    }
    # from holds every entry secret but those it knows public, so the join knows public only what both do
    var kept: vector.Vector[u64] = vector.init[u64](w.a);
    for (i < from.entries.len) {
        val k: u64 = from.entries.data[i];
        if (!entry_secret(into, k)) {
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](?kept, k);
            if (sel pushed.err) {
                vector.dnit[u64](?kept);
                ret failed[bool](pushed.err);
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    changed = !into.except || kept.len != into.entries.len;
    vector.dnit[u64](?into.entries);
    into.entries = kept;
    into.except  = true;
    ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{changed};
}

# `from` merged into the point at `to`, which is the version of a register the two disagree on, and a register's
# offset the two disagree on known no longer
# ---
# ret: whether the point at `to` changed, none when the two hold operand stacks of different heights
fun merge(w: *Walk, into: *Point, from: *Point, to: usize) res[opt[bool], A.Error] {
    if (into.stack.len != from.stack.len) { ret res[opt[bool], A.Error].ok{opt[bool].none{}}; }
    var changed: bool  = false;
    var i:       usize = 0;
    for (i < w.words) {
        val both: u64 = into.taint.data[i] | from.taint.data[i];
        if (both != into.taint.data[i]) { changed = true; }
        into.taint.data[i] = both;
        i                  = i + 1;
    }
    val joined: u64 = to::u64 * 2 + 2;
    i = 0;
    for (i < into.versions.len) {
        if (into.versions.data[i] != from.versions.data[i] && into.versions.data[i] != joined) {
            into.versions.data[i] = joined;
            changed               = true;
        }
        val f: *Frame = ?into.frames.data[i];
        if (f.known && (!from.frames.data[i].known || from.frames.data[i].offset != f.offset)) {
            @f      = UNKNOWN;
            changed = true;
        }
        val fo: *Formed = ?into.formed.data[i];
        if (fo.piece != fixup.NO_PIECE && !same_form(fo, ?from.formed.data[i])) {
            @fo     = UNFORMED;
            changed = true;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < from.held.len) {
        val before: usize        = into.held.len;
        val held:   err[A.Error] = hold(into, from.held.data[i]);
        if (sel held.err)            { ret failed[opt[bool]](held.err); }
        if (into.held.len != before) { changed = true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    # an extent is known public in the join only when it is on both paths
    var kept: usize = 0;
    i = 0;
    for (i < into.public.len) {
        var both: bool  = false;
        var k:    usize = 0;
        for (k < from.public.len) {
            if (same(?into.public.data[i], ?from.public.data[k])) { both = true; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        if (both) {
            into.public.data[kept] = into.public.data[i];
            kept                   = kept + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    if (kept != into.public.len) {
        vector.truncate[Held](?into.public, kept);
        changed = true;
    }
    if (from.anywhere && !into.anywhere) {
        into.anywhere = true;
        changed       = true;
        i             = 0;
        for (i < from.spared.len) {
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?into.spared, from.spared.data[i]);
            if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[opt[bool]](pushed.err); }
            i = i + 1;
        }
    }
    or (from.anywhere) {
        val narrowed: res[bool, A.Error] = narrow(w, ?into.spared, ?from.spared);
        if (sel narrowed.err) { ret failed[opt[bool]](narrowed.err); }
        if (narrowed.ok)      { changed = true; }
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < into.stack.len) {
        if (from.stack.data[i] && !into.stack.data[i]) {
            into.stack.data[i] = true;
            changed            = true;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    val entries: res[bool, A.Error] = merge_entries(w, into, from);
    if (sel entries.err) { ret failed[opt[bool]](entries.err); }
    if (entries.ok)      { changed = true; }
    var keep: bool = true;
    if (sel into.config.some) {
        keep = false;
        if (sel from.config.some) { keep = from.config.some.bits == into.config.some.bits; }
    }
    if (!keep) {
        into.config = opt[config.State].none{};
        changed     = true;
    }
    ret res[opt[bool], A.Error].ok{opt[bool].some{changed}};
}

# the state `p` reaching the instruction at `to`: its point made or merged into, and `to` queued when it changed
# ---
# ret: false when the point at `to` holds an operand stack of another height than `p`
fun reach(w: *Walk, p: *Point, to: usize) res[bool, A.Error] {
    val at: u32 = w.points.data[to];
    if (at == NO_POINT) {
        val made: res[Point, A.Error] = copy(w, p);
        if (sel made.err) { ret failed[bool](made.err); }
        w.points.data[to] = w.states.len::u32;
        val kept: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Point](?w.states, made.ok);
        if (sel kept.err) { ret failed[bool](kept.err); }
    }
    or {
        val merged: res[opt[bool], A.Error] = merge(w, ?w.states.data[at], p, to);
        if (sel merged.err)     { ret failed[bool](merged.err); }
        if (sel merged.ok.none) { ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{false}; }
        if (!merged.ok.some)    { ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{true}; }
    }
    val queued: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[usize](?w.work, to);
    if (sel queued.err) { ret failed[bool](queued.err); }
    ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{true};
}

fun row_index(w: *Walk, reg: register.Id) opt[u32] {
    if (reg == register.NONE) { ret opt[u32].none{}; }
    ret register.index_of(w.file, reg);
}

# whether register `reg` may hold a secret under `p`: its row, or any member of a tuple
fun tainted(w: *Walk, p: *Point, reg: register.Id) bool {
    val at: opt[u32] = row_index(w, reg);
    if (sel at.none) { ret false; }
    ret secret_row(w, p, at.some);
}

# whether row `at` may hold a secret under `p`: its own bit, or a tuple's members'
fun secret_row(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: u32) bool {
    val r: *register.Register = ?w.file.registers[at];
    if (!register.tuple(r)) { ret bit_of(p.taint.data, at); }
    var k: u32 = 0;
    for (k < r.members.len) {
        if (bit_of(p.taint.data, r.members.at[k])) { ret true; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether row `at` holds storage the walk keeps secrecy of: neither reading zero nor a tuple, whose members hold its
fun stored(w: *Walk, at: u32) bool {
    val r: *register.Register = ?w.file.registers[at];
    ret (r.flags & register.ZERO) == 0 && !register.tuple(r);
}

# the stack pointer's row: the register the canonical frame address of the first architecture of the code's set the
# context enters is stated from, effect.NO_ROW when none has call frames
fun stack_row(file: *register.File, code: *Code, ctx: *state.Context) u32 {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < code.set.arches.len) {
        val a: *set.Arch = ?code.set.arches.at[i];
        if (a.frame != nil && state.admits(ctx, a.enters)) {
            if (file.register_count == 0) { ret effect.NO_ROW; }
            val row: opt[u32] = register.index_of(file, a.frame.cfa_register);
            if (sel row.some) { ret row.some; }
            ret effect.NO_ROW;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret effect.NO_ROW;
}

# the architecture of the code's set the context enters, its first, nil for none
fun arch_of(code: *Code, ctx: *state.Context) *mink_arch.Arch {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < code.set.arches.len) {
        val a: *set.Arch = ?code.set.arches.at[i];
        if (state.admits(ctx, a.enters)) { ret a.arch; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret nil;
}

# whether register row `row` holds storage of its own as wide as the stack pointer's, so the value it holds may be a
# known offset from it
fun wide(w: *Walk, row: u32) bool {
    if (w.stack == effect.NO_ROW || row >= w.file.register_count) { ret false; }
    val r:  *register.Register = ?w.file.registers[row];
    val sp: *register.Register = ?w.file.registers[w.stack];
    val rw: quantity.Scaled    = w.file.classes[r.class].width;
    val sw: quantity.Scaled    = w.file.classes[sp.class].width;
    ret stored(w, row) && rw.fixed == sw.fixed && rw.per == sw.per && rw.scale == sw.scale && r.count.fixed == 1 && r.count.per == 0;
}

# the extent of `length` bytes at `offset` off the value register row `row` holds under `p`: off the stack pointer's
# value on entry when the walk knows the row's offset from it, else off that version of the row's value
fun rebase(w: *Walk, p: *Point, row: u32, offset: i64, length: u64) Held {
    val f: Frame = p.frames.data[row];
    if (f.known) { ret Held{base: w.stack, version: ENTRY, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: f.offset + offset, length: length}; }
    ret Held{base: row, version: p.versions.data[row], symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: offset, length: length};
}

# the registers `ins` writes as a stated function of what it reads into `w.derived`, with their inputs' secrecy under
# `p`, and those it gives a known offset into `w.moved`: each relation of its row, whose register written holds the one
# it reads plus a number no secret decides and no site fills, of a known offset where that one has one and both are as
# wide as the stack pointer, and the stack pointer's own change its effect states, its value before plus the delta's
# operand, but where an operand names the stack pointer
fun moves(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *walk.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint) err[A.Error] {
    vector.truncate[Moved](?w.moved, 0);
    vector.truncate[Derived](?w.derived, 0);
    val e:      *effect.Effect = ins.inst.row.effect;
    val values: operand.Values = operand.Values{at: ins.inst.values, len: ins.inst.count};
    var i:      u32            = 0;
    for (i < e.relations.len) {
        var got: opt[effect.Affine] = effect.affine(w.file, ?e.relations.at[i], values);
        # a number a site fills is no value until the link
        if (relation_sited(w, ?e.relations.at[i])) { got = opt[effect.Affine].none{}; }
        if (sel got.some) {
            val to:   opt[u32] = row_index(w, got.some.to);
            val from: opt[u32] = row_index(w, got.some.from);
            if (sel to.some) {
                if (sel from.some) {
                    val derived: err[A.Error] = derive(w, to.some, secret_row(w, p, from.some));
                    if (sel derived.err) { ret derived; }
                    val f: Frame = p.frames.data[from.some];
                    if (w.stack != effect.NO_ROW && f.known && wide(w, to.some) && wide(w, from.some)) {
                        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Moved](?w.moved, Moved{row: to.some, offset: f.offset + got.some.by});
                        if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    if (w.stack == effect.NO_ROW) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
    val st: effect.Stack = fp.stack;
    if (sel st.delta) {
        val f:      Frame = p.frames.data[w.stack];
        var bytes:  i64   = st.delta.bytes::i64;
        var known:  bool  = f.known;
        var stated: bool  = true;
        var secret: bool  = secret_row(w, p, w.stack);
        if (st.delta.operand != field.NO_OPERAND) {
            known  = false;
            stated = false;
            if (st.delta.operand::u32 < ins.inst.count) {
                val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[st.delta.operand];
                if (sel v.immediate) {
                    bytes  = bytes + v.immediate;
                    known  = f.known;
                    stated = true;
                }
                or (sel v.register) {
                    secret = secret || tainted(w, p, v.register);
                    stated = true;
                }
            }
        }
        # an operand naming the stack pointer may write it from data, as x86 `pop rsp`
        var op: u32 = 0;
        for (stated && op < ins.inst.count) {
            val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[op];
            if (sel v.register) {
                val at: opt[u32] = row_index(w, v.register);
                if (sel at.some) {
                    val sharing: res[bool, A.Error] = shares(w, at.some, w.stack);
                    if (sel sharing.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{sharing.err}; }
                    if (sharing.ok)      { stated = false; }
                }
            }
            op = op + 1;
        }
        if (stated) {
            val derived: err[A.Error] = derive(w, w.stack, secret);
            if (sel derived.err) { ret derived; }
        }
        if (known) {
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Moved](?w.moved, Moved{row: w.stack, offset: f.offset + bytes});
            if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
        }
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# row `row` into `w.derived` as written from inputs of which any is secret when `secret` is, one a relation and the
# stack's delta both write taking either's
fun derive(w: *Walk, row: u32, secret: bool) err[A.Error] {
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < w.derived.len) {
        if (w.derived.data[k].row == row) {
            w.derived.data[k].secret = w.derived.data[k].secret || secret;
            ret err[A.Error].ok{};
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Derived](?w.derived, Derived{row: row, secret: secret});
    if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# whether register row `row` the instruction walked writes takes secrecy of its own: its inputs' where `w.derived`
# holds it, else `value`, whether anything the instruction reads is secret
fun written_secret(w: *Walk, row: u32, value: bool) bool {
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < w.derived.len) {
        if (w.derived.data[k].row == row) { ret w.derived.data[k].secret; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret value;
}

# the rows a register value of operand `op` covers marked in `into`, and whether any of them is secret under `p`. a
# grouped value covers the registers its operand's groups do, an address register one
fun mark_register(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *walk.Decoded, op: u8, reg: register.Id, grouped: bool, cfg: config.Configured, into: *u64) bool {
    val at: opt[u32] = row_index(w, reg);
    if (sel at.none) { ret false; }
    var count: u32 = 1;
    if (grouped) {
        val covers: effect.Answer[u32] = footprint.covers(ins.inst.row, op, w.ctx, cfg);
        if (sel covers.decided) {
            if (covers.decided > 1) { count = covers.decided; }
        }
    }
    var secret: bool = false;
    var k:      u32  = 0;
    for (k < count && at.some + k < w.file.register_count) {
        set_bit(into, at.some + k, true);
        if (secret_row(w, p, at.some + k)) { secret = true; }
        # a tuple's members are the operand's registers as much as the tuple is
        val r: *register.Register = ?w.file.registers[at.some + k];
        var j: u32                = 0;
        for (j < r.members.len) {
            set_bit(into, r.members.at[j], true);
            j = j + 1;
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret secret;
}

# whether a register value of operand `op` is secret under `p`, its rows marked in `into`: a register, every member of
# a list, and a memory value's address registers, which are marked but are no data of the operand
fun operand_secret(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *walk.Decoded, op: u8, cfg: config.Configured, into: *u64) bool {
    val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[op];
    if (sel v.register) { ret mark_register(w, p, ins, op, v.register, true, cfg, into); }
    if (sel v.list) {
        var secret: bool = false;
        var i:      u32  = 0;
        for (i < v.list.len) {
            val m: operand.Value = v.list.at[i];
            if (sel m.register && mark_register(w, p, ins, op, m.register, false, cfg, into)) { secret = true; }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        ret secret;
    }
    # the address registers are named, and a secret in them is refused as an address, not as the operand's data
    if (sel v.memory) {
        mark_register(w, p, ins, op, v.memory.base, false, cfg, into);
        mark_register(w, p, ins, op, v.memory.index, false, cfg, into);
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether some register of operand `op`'s value is secret under `p`, its address registers included
fun names_secret(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *walk.Decoded, op: u8) bool {
    if (op == field.NO_OPERAND || op::u32 >= ins.inst.count) { ret false; }
    val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[op];
    if (sel v.register) { ret tainted(w, p, v.register); }
    if (sel v.memory)   { ret tainted(w, p, v.memory.base) || tainted(w, p, v.memory.index); }
    if (sel v.list) {
        var i: u32 = 0;
        for (i < v.list.len) {
            val m: operand.Value = v.list.at[i];
            if (sel m.register && tainted(w, p, m.register)) { ret true; }
            i = i + 1;
        }
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether the value the instruction pops at depth `pop` less one may hold a secret under `p`, which holds the
# instruction's pops on top of its stack. none for 0, and the ordered read holds every depth to what the instruction pops
fun popped_secret(p: *Point, pop: u8) bool {
    if (pop == 0) { ret false; }
    ret p.stack.data[p.stack.len - pop::usize];
}

# the bytes access width `width` covers, 0 when the walk does not know them: a width scaling with a quantity, or a
# count no element fixes
fun bytes_of(width: *effect.Width) u64 {
    val count: effect.Count = width.count;
    if (!sel count.one || width.element.per != 0 || width.element.fixed == 0) { ret 0; }
    ret (width.element.fixed::u64 + 7) / 8;
}

# the extent an address of `ins` touches, from the operand that is or holds it plus the immediates of the further
# operands `forming` names, or the register row `base` when none, plus the access's own `offset`, named off the stack
# pointer when the walk knows that register's offset from it, or off a symbol's address when the sites place it there
# (`address_formed`). an address a further operand forms that is no immediate, as a risc-v stride, is placed nowhere, and
# so is one a site fills that the sites do not place, whose number is no address until the link
fun placed(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *walk.Decoded, op: u8, base: u32, forming: operand.Positions, offset: i64, length: u64, touch: *Touch) {
    touch.operand   = field.NO_OPERAND;
    touch.at        = UNPLACED;
    touch.at.offset = offset;
    touch.at.length = length;
    var formed: Formed = UNFORMED;
    var sited:  bool   = false;
    var added:  i64    = 0;
    if (op != field.NO_OPERAND && op::u32 < ins.inst.count) {
        val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[op];
        sited = has_site(w, op);
        if (sel v.memory) {
            touch.operand   = op;
            touch.at.offset = touch.at.offset + v.memory.disp;
            val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, v.memory.base);
            if (sel row.some) { touch.at.base = row.some; }
            formed = address_formed(w, p, ins, op);
        }
        or (sel v.register) {
            val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, v.register);
            if (sel row.some) {
                touch.at.base = row.some;
                formed        = whole_of(p.formed.data[row.some]);
            }
        }
        or (sel v.relative) { formed = address_formed(w, p, ins, op); }
        var k: u32 = 0;
        for (k < ins.inst.count && k < 32) {
            if ((forming & (1::u32 << k)) != 0) {
                val f: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[k];
                if (has_site(w, k::u8)) {
                    sited  = true;
                    formed = UNFORMED;
                }
                if (sel f.immediate) {
                    touch.at.offset = touch.at.offset + f.immediate;
                    added           = added + f.immediate;
                }
                or {
                    touch.at.base = effect.NO_ROW;
                    formed        = UNFORMED;
                }
            }
            k = k + 1;
        }
    }
    or {
        touch.at.base = base;
        if (base != effect.NO_ROW) { formed = whole_of(p.formed.data[base]); }
    }
    touch.row     = touch.at.base;
    touch.rebased = 0;
    if (formed.piece == fixup.WHOLE) {
        touch.at  = Held{base: effect.NO_ROW, version: ENTRY, symbol: formed.symbol, slot: formed.slot, offset: formed.offset + offset + added, length: length};
        touch.row = effect.NO_ROW;
        ret;
    }
    if (sited) {
        touch.at.base = effect.NO_ROW;
        touch.row     = effect.NO_ROW;
    }
    if (touch.at.base != effect.NO_ROW) {
        val h: Held = rebase(w, p, touch.at.base, touch.at.offset, touch.at.length);
        touch.rebased = h.offset - touch.at.offset;
        touch.at      = h;
    }
}

# the site the caller states for operand `op` of the instruction starting at `at`, none for none
fun site_at(w: *Walk, at: usize, op: u8) opt[*Site] {
    if (at >= w.sited.len) { ret opt[*Site].none{}; }
    var i: u32 = w.sited.data[at];
    for (i != NO_POINT && i < w.code.sites.len) {
        val st: *Site = ?w.code.sites.at[i];
        if (st.at != at::u64) { ret opt[*Site].none{}; }
        if (st.operand == op) { ret opt[*Site].some{st}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret opt[*Site].none{};
}

# whether a site fills operand `op` of the instruction walked
fun has_site(w: *Walk, op: u8) bool {
    val st: opt[*Site] = site_at(w, w.at, op);
    ret sel st.some;
}

# the capabilities of the relocation kind site `st`'s fixup kind is bound to on the architecture the walk runs under,
# none for a kind bound to none there, as a local kind
fun site_caps(w: *Walk, st: *Site) opt[reloc.Caps] {
    if (w.arch == nil) { ret opt[reloc.Caps].none{}; }
    val all: fixup.Bindings = w.code.set.bindings;
    var i:   u32            = 0;
    for (i < all.len) {
        val b: *fixup.Binding = ?all.at[i];
        if (b.fixup == st.fixup && fixup.binds(b, w.arch)) { ret opt[reloc.Caps].some{reloc.caps(b.kind)}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret opt[reloc.Caps].none{};
}

# `f` when it is a symbol's address, else UNFORMED
fun whole_of(f: Formed) Formed {
    if (f.piece == fixup.WHOLE) { ret f; }
    ret UNFORMED;
}

# whether `x` and `y` hold one part of one address
fun same_form(x: *Formed, y: *Formed) bool {
    ret x.piece == y.piece && x.symbol == y.symbol && x.offset == y.offset && x.slot == y.slot && x.partnered == y.partnered && x.site == y.site;
}

# what the operand site `st` fills holds of its symbol's address alone, by the part its fixup kind holds: the address,
# a high part, or UNFORMED for a low part, which completes a high one, or a kind the set states no part of
fun site_formed(w: *Walk, st: *Site) Formed {
    if (st.symbol == operand.NO_SYMBOL) { ret UNFORMED; }
    val piece: fixup.Piece     = fixup.piece_of(w.code.set.parts, st.fixup);
    val caps:  opt[reloc.Caps] = site_caps(w, st);
    if (sel caps.none) { ret UNFORMED; }
    val slot: bool = (caps.some & reloc.GOT) != 0;
    if (piece == fixup.WHOLE) { ret Formed{piece: fixup.WHOLE, symbol: st.symbol, offset: st.addend, slot: slot, partnered: false, site: 0}; }
    if (piece == fixup.HIGH) {
        val partnered: bool = (caps.some & reloc.PC) != 0 && (caps.some & reloc.PAGE) == 0;
        ret Formed{piece: fixup.HIGH, symbol: st.symbol, offset: st.addend, slot: slot, partnered: partnered, site: st.at};
    }
    ret UNFORMED;
}

# the address high part `high` and the low part site `st` fills make, UNFORMED unless they are of one address: a low
# part naming a partner completes the high part its partner's instruction formed, and any other one of the same symbol,
# addend and slot that no partner completes
fun completed(w: *Walk, high: Formed, st: *Site) Formed {
    if (high.piece != fixup.HIGH || fixup.piece_of(w.code.set.parts, st.fixup) != fixup.LOW) { ret UNFORMED; }
    val caps: opt[reloc.Caps] = site_caps(w, st);
    if (sel caps.none) { ret UNFORMED; }
    if ((caps.some & reloc.PARTNER) != 0) {
        if (!high.partnered || high.site != st.partner) { ret UNFORMED; }
    }
    or {
        val slot: bool = (caps.some & reloc.GOT) != 0;
        if (high.partnered || high.symbol != st.symbol || high.offset != st.addend || high.slot != slot) { ret UNFORMED; }
    }
    ret Formed{piece: fixup.WHOLE, symbol: high.symbol, offset: high.offset, slot: high.slot, partnered: false, site: 0};
}

# the symbol's address the address operand `op` of `ins` forms under `p`, UNFORMED for none the sites place: a site of
# the address whole in a relative operand or an address of no base, as a rip-relative or absolute one, a site of a
# low part added to a base register holding its high part, or a base register holding an address plus a displacement
# no site fills. an address with an index or written back after the access is placed by no symbol
fun address_formed(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *walk.Decoded, op: u8) Formed {
    if (op == field.NO_OPERAND || op::u32 >= ins.inst.count) { ret UNFORMED; }
    val v:  operand.Value = ins.inst.values[op];
    val st: opt[*Site]    = site_at(w, w.at, op);
    if (sel v.relative) {
        if (sel st.some) { ret whole_of(site_formed(w, st.some)); }
        ret UNFORMED;
    }
    if (!sel v.memory) { ret UNFORMED; }
    val m: operand.Address = v.memory;
    if (m.index != register.NONE)                                                                { ret UNFORMED; }
    if (m.mode != operand.OFFSET && m.mode != operand.PREINDEX && m.mode != operand.RELATIVE_PC) { ret UNFORMED; }
    if (m.base == register.NONE || m.mode == operand.RELATIVE_PC) {
        if (sel st.some) { ret whole_of(site_formed(w, st.some)); }
        ret UNFORMED;
    }
    val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, m.base);
    if (sel row.none) { ret UNFORMED; }
    var f: Formed = p.formed.data[row.some];
    if (sel st.some)            { ret completed(w, f, st.some); }
    if (f.piece != fixup.WHOLE) { ret UNFORMED; }
    f.offset = f.offset + m.disp;
    ret f;
}

# the register a relation of `ins` writes, register.NONE for none it names
fun related_to(w: *Walk, ins: *walk.Decoded, rel: *effect.Relation) register.Id {
    if (sel rel.to.operand) {
        if (rel.to.operand::u32 >= ins.inst.count) { ret register.NONE; }
        val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[rel.to.operand];
        if (sel v.register) { ret v.register; }
        ret register.NONE;
    }
    if (sel rel.to.row) {
        if (rel.to.row >= w.file.register_count) { ret register.NONE; }
        ret register.id_of(?w.file.registers[rel.to.row]);
    }
    ret register.NONE;
}

# what relation `rel` of `ins` leaves its register holding of a symbol's address under `p`: what a site of the operand
# it forms its value from holds, the address a lea's operand forms, a low part a site fills added to the high part its
# register holds, or an address its register holds plus a number no site fills, as a copy or an add of an immediate
fun relation_formed(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *walk.Decoded, rel: *effect.Relation) Formed {
    if (sel rel.holds.formed) {
        val st: opt[*Site] = site_at(w, w.at, rel.holds.formed);
        if (sel st.some) { ret site_formed(w, st.some); }
        ret UNFORMED;
    }
    if (!sel rel.holds.offset) { ret UNFORMED; }
    val o: effect.Offset = rel.holds.offset;
    if (sel o.from.base) { ret whole_of(address_formed(w, p, ins, o.from.base)); }
    var from: register.Id = register.NONE;
    if (sel o.from.operand) {
        if (o.from.operand::u32 < ins.inst.count) {
            val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[o.from.operand];
            if (sel v.register) { from = v.register; }
        }
    }
    or (sel o.from.row) {
        if (o.from.row < w.file.register_count) { from = register.id_of(?w.file.registers[o.from.row]); }
    }
    val src: opt[u32] = row_index(w, from);
    if (sel src.none) { ret UNFORMED; }
    var f: Formed = p.formed.data[src.some];
    if (sel o.by.immediate) {
        val st: opt[*Site] = site_at(w, w.at, o.by.immediate);
        if (sel st.some) {
            if (o.negated || o.shift != field.NO_OPERAND || o.constant != 0) { ret UNFORMED; }
            ret completed(w, f, st.some);
        }
    }
    if (f.piece != fixup.WHOLE) { ret UNFORMED; }
    val values: operand.Values     = operand.Values{at: ins.inst.values, len: ins.inst.count};
    val got:    opt[effect.Affine] = effect.affine(w.file, rel, values);
    if (sel got.none) { ret UNFORMED; }
    f.offset = f.offset + got.some.by;
    ret f;
}

# whether a site fills an operand relation `rel` adds or starts from, whose number is no value until the link
fun relation_sited(w: *Walk, rel: *effect.Relation) bool {
    if (!sel rel.holds.offset) { ret false; }
    val o: effect.Offset = rel.holds.offset;
    if (sel o.by.immediate) {
        if (has_site(w, o.by.immediate)) { ret true; }
    }
    if (sel o.by.displacement) {
        if (has_site(w, o.by.displacement)) { ret true; }
    }
    if (sel o.from.base) {
        if (has_site(w, o.from.base)) { ret true; }
    }
    ret false;
}

# the row of the one register operand `ins` writes, none for none or more than one
fun written_row(w: *Walk, ins: *walk.Decoded) opt[u32] {
    val r:     *operand.Operand = ins.inst.row.operands.at;
    var found: u32              = effect.NO_ROW;
    var count: u32              = 0;
    var op:    u32              = 0;
    for (op < ins.inst.count) {
        val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[op];
        if (sel v.register) {
            if ((r[op].role & operand.WRITE) != 0) {
                count = count + 1;
                found = row_or_none(w, v.register);
            }
        }
        op = op + 1;
    }
    if (count != 1 || found == effect.NO_ROW) { ret opt[u32].none{}; }
    ret opt[u32].some{found};
}

# the registers `ins` gives a symbol's address or a part of one under `p` into `w.forming`: each its row's relations
# write as wide as the stack pointer, and the one register a load of a got slot alone writes, which takes the slot's
# symbol's address. read where the instruction starts, once `w.touches` holds its touches
fun formings(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *walk.Decoded) err[A.Error] {
    vector.truncate[Forming](?w.forming, 0);
    if (w.code.sites.len == 0) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
    val e: *effect.Effect = ins.inst.row.effect;
    var i: u32            = 0;
    for (i < e.relations.len) {
        val rel: *effect.Relation = ?e.relations.at[i];
        val row: opt[u32]         = row_index(w, related_to(w, ins, rel));
        if (sel row.some) {
            if (wide(w, row.some)) {
                val f: Formed = relation_formed(w, p, ins, rel);
                if (f.piece != fixup.NO_PIECE) {
                    val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Forming](?w.forming, Forming{row: row.some, formed: f});
                    if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
                }
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    if (w.forming.len != 0 || w.touches.len != 1) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
    val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[0];
    if (!t.reads || t.writes || !symbolic(?t.at) || !t.at.slot || t.at.offset != 0) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
    val row: opt[u32] = written_row(w, ins);
    if (sel row.some) {
        if (wide(w, row.some)) {
            val f:      Formed              = Formed{piece: fixup.WHOLE, symbol: t.at.symbol, offset: 0, slot: false, partnered: false, site: 0};
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Forming](?w.forming, Forming{row: row.some, formed: f});
            if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
        }
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# the bytes the access of memory operand `o` holding address `m` covers, its width of one value, 0 when the walk does
# not know them: a width the operand does not state, more than one value, or an element broadcast from part of it
fun operand_bytes(o: *operand.Operand, m: operand.Address) u64 {
    if (o.width == 0 || o.quantity != operand.ONE || m.broadcast != 0) { ret 0; }
    ret (o.width::u64 + 7) / 8;
}

# the refusal of a secret in what decides an access's count `count` under `p`: the register at its row, its operand or
# the value it pops, naming the operand when one decides it. none for a count nothing the instruction reads decides
fun count_secret(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *walk.Decoded, count: effect.Count) opt[ct.Refusal] {
    var secret: bool = false;
    var op:     u8   = field.NO_OPERAND;
    if (sel count.register) { secret = bit_of(p.taint.data, count.register); }
    or (sel count.operand) {
        op     = count.operand;
        secret = names_secret(w, p, ins, op);
    }
    or (sel count.popped) { secret = popped_secret(p, count.popped + 1); }
    if (!secret)          { ret opt[ct.Refusal].none{}; }
    ret opt[ct.Refusal].some{ct.refusal(ct.MEMORY, op)};
}

# the refusal of a secret in the index `x` of an access adds to its address under `p`: the register at its row or its
# operand, naming the operand when one holds it. none for no index, or one of no form the walk knows, which it places
# nowhere
fun index_secret(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *walk.Decoded, x: *effect.Index) opt[ct.Refusal] {
    if (sel x.register) {
        if (x.register.at != effect.NO_ROW && bit_of(p.taint.data, x.register.at)) { ret opt[ct.Refusal].some{ct.refusal(ct.MEMORY, field.NO_OPERAND)}; }
    }
    if (sel x.operand) {
        val op: u8 = x.operand.at::u8;
        if (names_secret(w, p, ins, op)) { ret opt[ct.Refusal].some{ct.refusal(ct.MEMORY, op)}; }
    }
    ret opt[ct.Refusal].none{};
}

fun found(r: ct.Refusal) res[opt[ct.Refusal], A.Error] {
    ret res[opt[ct.Refusal], A.Error].ok{opt[ct.Refusal].some{r}};
}

# whether the walk places the extent `h` in an object it names: off a symbol's address, or in the frame off the stack
# pointer's value on entry
fun pinned(w: *Walk, h: *Held) bool {
    ret symbolic(h) || (w.stack != effect.NO_ROW && h.base == w.stack && h.version == ENTRY);
}

# whether access seed `a` names touch `t`
fun names_touch(a: *Access, t: *Touch) bool {
    if (sel a.access.operand) { ret a.access.operand != field.NO_OPERAND && a.access.operand == t.named; }
    if (sel a.access.index)   { ret a.access.index == t.index; }
    ret false;
}

# touch `t` of the instruction walked seeded by the access seeds naming it, secret when any of them is, for a touch the
# walk does not place (`pinned`)
fun take_seed(w: *Walk, t: *Touch) {
    if (pinned(w, ?t.at)) { ret; }
    var i: u32 = w.stated.data[w.at];
    for (i != NO_POINT) {
        val sd: Seed = w.secrets.at[i];
        if (sel sd.access) {
            var a: Access = sd.access;
            if (names_touch(?a, t)) {
                t.seeded = true;
                if (a.secret) { t.secret = true; }
            }
        }
        i = w.sowing.data[i];
    }
}

# whether each access seed at the instruction walked names one of its touches, placed or not
fun accessed(w: *Walk) bool {
    var i: u32 = w.stated.data[w.at];
    for (i != NO_POINT) {
        val sd: Seed = w.secrets.at[i];
        if (sel sd.access) {
            var a:     Access = sd.access;
            var found: bool   = false;
            var k:     usize  = 0;
            for (k < w.touches.len) {
                if (names_touch(?a, ?w.touches.data[k])) { found = true; }
                k = k + 1;
            }
            if (!found) { ret false; }
        }
        i = w.sowing.data[i];
    }
    ret true;
}

# whether touch `t` reads what may hold a secret under `p`: what its access seed states, else what the extents say
fun reads_secret(w: *Walk, p: *Point, t: *Touch) bool {
    if (!t.reads) { ret false; }
    if (t.seeded) { ret t.secret; }
    ret secret_at(w, p, ?t.at);
}

# the memory accesses of `ins` gathered into `w.touches`: each its footprint states, then each memory operand none of
# them names. a secret in what forms an address or a value popped as one, or in what decides its count of elements, is
# refused
fun touches(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *walk.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint) res[opt[ct.Refusal], A.Error] {
    vector.truncate[Touch](?w.touches, 0);
    val r: *operand.Operand = ins.inst.row.operands.at;
    var i: u32              = 0;
    for (i < fp.memory.len) {
        val acc:  *effect.Access = ?fp.memory.at[i];
        var role: operand.Role   = acc.role;
        if (role == operand.NONE && acc.operand != field.NO_OPERAND && acc.operand::u32 < ins.inst.count) { role = r[acc.operand].role; }
        var t: Touch = Touch{reads: (role & operand.READ) != 0, writes: (role & operand.WRITE) != 0, operand: field.NO_OPERAND, at: UNPLACED, row: effect.NO_ROW, rebased: 0, named: acc.operand, index: i, seeded: false, secret: false};
        placed(w, p, ins, acc.operand, acc.base, acc.forming, acc.offset, bytes_of(?acc.width), ?t);
        # an address an index adds to is placed nowhere, as xlat's rbx plus al
        if (!sel acc.index.none) {
            t.at.base   = effect.NO_ROW;
            t.at.symbol = operand.NO_SYMBOL;
            t.at.slot   = false;
            t.row       = effect.NO_ROW;
            t.rebased   = 0;
        }
        take_seed(w, ?t);
        val indexed: opt[ct.Refusal] = index_secret(w, p, ins, ?acc.index);
        if (sel indexed.some)                                                          { ret found(indexed.some); }
        if (names_secret(w, p, ins, acc.operand))                                      { ret found(ct.refusal(ct.MEMORY, acc.operand)); }
        if (acc.base != effect.NO_ROW && bit_of(p.taint.data, acc.base))               { ret found(ct.refusal(ct.MEMORY, field.NO_OPERAND)); }
        if (acc.governor != field.NO_OPERAND && names_secret(w, p, ins, acc.governor)) { ret found(ct.refusal(ct.MEMORY, acc.governor)); }
        if (popped_secret(p, acc.pop))                                                 { ret found(ct.refusal(ct.MEMORY, field.NO_OPERAND)); }
        val counted: opt[ct.Refusal] = count_secret(w, p, ins, acc.width.count);
        if (sel counted.some) { ret found(counted.some); }
        var k: u32 = 0;
        for (k < ins.inst.count && k < 32) {
            if ((acc.forming & (1::u32 << k)) != 0 && names_secret(w, p, ins, k::u8)) { ret found(ct.refusal(ct.MEMORY, k::u8)); }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Touch](?w.touches, t);
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[opt[ct.Refusal]](pushed.err); }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    var op: u32 = 0;
    for (op < ins.inst.count) {
        val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[op];
        if (sel v.memory) {
            var stated: bool = false;
            var k:      u32  = 0;
            for (k < fp.memory.len) {
                if (fp.memory.at[k].operand::u32 == op) { stated = true; }
                k = k + 1;
            }
            if (names_secret(w, p, ins, op::u8)) { ret found(ct.refusal(ct.MEMORY, op::u8)); }
            if (!stated) {
                val role: operand.Role = r[op].role;
                var t:    Touch        = Touch{reads: (role & operand.READ) != 0, writes: (role & operand.WRITE) != 0, operand: field.NO_OPERAND, at: UNPLACED, row: effect.NO_ROW, rebased: 0, named: op::u8, index: NO_ACCESS, seeded: false, secret: false};
                placed(w, p, ins, op::u8, effect.NO_ROW, 0, 0, operand_bytes(?r[op], v.memory), ?t);
                take_seed(w, ?t);
                val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Touch](?w.touches, t);
                if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[opt[ct.Refusal]](pushed.err); }
            }
        }
        op = op + 1;
    }
    ret res[opt[ct.Refusal], A.Error].ok{opt[ct.Refusal].none{}};
}

# the latency refusal of a secret in an input of `ins`, none when its timing depends on no input holding one under the
# walk's context, as `ct.latency` decides for each: an operand it reads, the data of a memory operand it reads, the
# data of an access no operand names, and a register no operand names that it reads
fun latency(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *walk.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint, secret: u32) opt[ct.Refusal] {
    val c:  *ct.Class        = ins.inst.row.ct;
    val r:  *operand.Operand = ins.inst.row.operands.at;
    var op: u32              = 0;
    for (op < ins.inst.count && op < 32) {
        if ((r[op].role & operand.READ) != 0) {
            var held: bool  = (secret & (1::u32 << op)) != 0;
            var k:    usize = 0;
            for (k < w.touches.len) {
                val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[k];
                if (t.operand::u32 == op && reads_secret(w, p, t)) { held = true; }
                k = k + 1;
            }
            if (held) {
                val refused: opt[ct.Refusal] = ct.latency(c, w.ctx, w.file, ct.Input.operand{op::u8});
                if (sel refused.some) { ret refused; }
            }
        }
        op = op + 1;
    }
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < w.touches.len) {
        val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[k];
        if (t.operand == field.NO_OPERAND && reads_secret(w, p, t)) {
            val refused: opt[ct.Refusal] = ct.latency(c, w.ctx, w.file, ct.Input.access{});
            if (sel refused.some) { ret refused; }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    var row: u32 = 0;
    for (row < w.file.register_count) {
        if (bit_of(fp.reads.data, row) && !bit_of(w.named.data, row) && bit_of(p.taint.data, row)) {
            val refused: opt[ct.Refusal] = ct.latency(c, w.ctx, w.file, ct.Input.register{register.id_of(?w.file.registers[row])});
            if (sel refused.some) { ret refused; }
        }
        row = row + 1;
    }
    ret opt[ct.Refusal].none{};
}

# the first operand of `ins` whose registers hold a secret, field.NO_OPERAND when none does
fun first_secret(secret: u32, count: u32) u8 {
    var op: u32 = 0;
    for (op < count && op < 32) {
        if ((secret & (1::u32 << op)) != 0) { ret op::u8; }
        op = op + 1;
    }
    ret field.NO_OPERAND;
}

# the control refusal of `ins`: a transfer that may fall through decided by a secret, or one to a target formed from
# one. `held` is whether what it reads but the values it pops is secret, and `stacked` whether a value it pops is.
# the values a transfer pops decide it only through the condition and the chooser its effect names, but for a
# conditional or indirect one that names neither, which every value it reads may decide
fun control(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *walk.Decoded, c: *effect.Control, held: bool, stacked: bool, secret: u32) opt[ct.Refusal] {
    if (c.transfer == effect.NONE || c.transfer == effect.MERGE) { ret opt[ct.Refusal].none{}; }
    if (c.conditional) {
        if (c.condition != 0) {
            if (popped_secret(p, c.condition)) { ret opt[ct.Refusal].some{ct.refusal(ct.CONTROL, field.NO_OPERAND)}; }
        }
        or (held || stacked) { ret opt[ct.Refusal].some{ct.refusal(ct.CONTROL, first_secret(secret, ins.inst.count))}; }
    }
    if (popped_secret(p, c.chooses)) { ret opt[ct.Refusal].some{ct.refusal(ct.CONTROL, field.NO_OPERAND)}; }
    if (c.target == effect.INDIRECT || (c.target == effect.UNTARGETED && c.transfer == effect.RETURN)) {
        if (c.operand == field.NO_OPERAND) {
            var decided: bool = held;
            if (c.target == effect.INDIRECT && c.chooses == 0) { decided = held || stacked; }
            if (decided)                                       { ret opt[ct.Refusal].some{ct.refusal(ct.CONTROL, field.NO_OPERAND)}; }
            ret opt[ct.Refusal].none{};
        }
        if (names_secret(w, p, ins, c.operand)) { ret opt[ct.Refusal].some{ct.refusal(ct.CONTROL, c.operand)}; }
        var k: usize = 0;
        for (k < w.touches.len) {
            val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[k];
            if (t.operand == c.operand && reads_secret(w, p, t)) { ret opt[ct.Refusal].some{ct.refusal(ct.CONTROL, c.operand)}; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
    }
    ret opt[ct.Refusal].none{};
}

# whether `a` and `b` are one type of a signature: one fixed type, one variable or one operand's types
fun same_ref(a: effect.TypeRef, b: effect.TypeRef) bool {
    if (sel a.fixed)    { ret sel b.fixed && b.fixed == a.fixed; }
    if (sel a.variable) { ret sel b.variable && b.variable == a.variable; }
    if (sel a.operand)  { ret sel b.operand && b.operand == a.operand; }
    if (sel a.results)  { ret sel b.results; }
    ret false;
}

# whether type `ref` of a signature is one it pushes again, of `sig`'s pushes
fun pushed_again(sig: *effect.Signature, ref: effect.TypeRef) bool {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < sig.pushes.len) {
        if (same_ref(sig.pushes.at[i], ref)) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# how many values the shape `s` of an instruction of signature `sig` pops
fun pop_count(w: *Walk, s: *Shape, sig: *effect.Signature) usize {
    var n: usize = 0;
    var i: u32   = 0;
    for (i < sig.pops.len) {
        n = n + w.counts.data[s.counts + i]::usize;
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret n;
}

# the key of the entry operand `op` of `ins` names, none for an operand holding no id
fun entry_key(ins: *walk.Decoded, op: u8) opt[u64] {
    if (op::u32 >= ins.inst.count || op::u32 >= ins.inst.row.operands.len) { ret opt[u64].none{}; }
    val shape: *operand.Shape = ?ins.inst.row.operands.at[op].shape;
    val v:     operand.Value  = ins.inst.values[op];
    if (sel shape.id) {
        if (sel v.id) { ret opt[u64].some{key(shape.id.space, v.id)}; }
    }
    ret opt[u64].none{};
}

# whether an entry `ins` reads through its operands may hold a secret under `p`. an operand holding no id may name
# any entry
fun entries_read(p: *Point, ins: *walk.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint) bool {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < fp.entries.len) {
        val n: *effect.Entry = ?fp.entries.at[i];
        if ((n.role & operand.READ) != 0) {
            val k: opt[u64] = entry_key(ins, n.operand);
            if (sel k.some) {
                if (entry_secret(p, k.some)) { ret true; }
            }
            or (any_entry(p)) { ret true; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# the values of the pop of `sig` of type `ref` copied into `w.carried`, the deepest first, from the pops of shape `s`
# on top of `p`'s stack, none when the instruction pops no value of that type
fun carry(w: *Walk, p: *Point, s: *Shape, sig: *effect.Signature, ref: effect.TypeRef) err[A.Error] {
    vector.truncate[bool](?w.carried, 0);
    var at: usize = p.stack.len - pop_count(w, s, sig);
    var i:  u32   = 0;
    for (i < sig.pops.len) {
        val n: usize = w.counts.data[s.counts + i]::usize;
        if (same_ref(sig.pops.at[i], ref)) {
            var k: usize = 0;
            for (k < n) {
                val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[bool](?w.carried, p.stack.data[at + k]);
                if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
                k = k + 1;
            }
            ret err[A.Error].ok{};
        }
        at = at + n;
        i  = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# what an instruction of a typed stream leaves secret, applied to `p`: the entries it writes take `value`, and its pops
# are replaced on the stack, by the params an opening instruction passes into its block as they are, else by its
# pushes, each a value a jump pops of the same type and count as it pushes, as br_if leaves the values its label
# takes, kept as it was, and every other taking `value`. a call, whose callee the walk does not read, leaves what it
# pushes, every entry and every address secret when anything is
fun apply_stream(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *walk.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint, s: *Shape, value: bool) err[A.Error] {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < fp.entries.len) {
        val n: *effect.Entry = ?fp.entries.at[i];
        if ((n.role & operand.WRITE) != 0) {
            val k: opt[u64] = entry_key(ins, n.operand);
            if (sel k.some) {
                val set: err[A.Error] = set_entry(p, k.some, value);
                if (sel set.err) { ret set; }
            }
            # a write through an operand holding no id may reach any entry
            or (value) {
                p.except = true;
                vector.truncate[u64](?p.entries, 0);
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    val sig:    *effect.Signature = ?fp.signature;
    val bottom: usize             = p.stack.len - pop_count(w, s, sig);
    vector.truncate[bool](?w.popped, 0);
    var k: usize = bottom;
    for (k < p.stack.len) {
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[bool](?w.popped, p.stack.data[k]);
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    vector.truncate[bool](?p.stack, bottom);
    if (effect.opens(fp.structure)) {
        var at: usize = 0;
        i = 0;
        for (i < sig.pops.len) {
            val n: usize = w.counts.data[s.counts + i]::usize;
            if (pushed_again(sig, sig.pops.at[i])) {
                k = 0;
                for (k < n) {
                    val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[bool](?p.stack, w.popped.data[at + k]);
                    if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
                    k = k + 1;
                }
            }
            at = at + n;
            i  = i + 1;
        }
        ret err[A.Error].ok{};
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < sig.pushes.len) {
        val n:    usize          = w.counts.data[s.counts + sig.pops.len + i]::usize;
        val ref:  effect.TypeRef = sig.pushes.at[i];
        var from: usize          = NO_OFFSET;
        if (fp.control.transfer == effect.JUMP) {
            var at: usize = 0;
            var j:  u32   = 0;
            for (j < sig.pops.len) {
                val m: usize = w.counts.data[s.counts + j]::usize;
                if (same_ref(sig.pops.at[j], ref) && m == n) { from = at; }
                at = at + m;
                j  = j + 1;
            }
        }
        k = 0;
        for (k < n) {
            var held: bool = value;
            if (from != NO_OFFSET) { held = w.popped.data[from + k]; }
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[bool](?p.stack, held);
            if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    if (fp.control.transfer == effect.CALL) {
        var secret: bool = value || p.anywhere || p.held.len > 0 || any_entry(p);
        k = 0;
        for (k < p.stack.len) {
            if (p.stack.data[k]) { secret = true; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        var word: usize = 0;
        for (word < w.words) {
            if (p.taint.data[word] != 0) { secret = true; }
            word = word + 1;
        }
        if (secret) {
            k = p.stack.len - push_count(w, s, sig);
            for (k < p.stack.len) {
                p.stack.data[k] = true;
                k               = k + 1;
            }
            p.except = true;
            vector.truncate[u64](?p.entries, 0);
            vector.truncate[Held](?p.public, 0);
            everywhere(p);
        }
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# how many values the shape `s` of an instruction of signature `sig` pushes
fun push_count(w: *Walk, s: *Shape, sig: *effect.Signature) usize {
    var n: usize = 0;
    var i: u32   = 0;
    for (i < sig.pushes.len) {
        n = n + w.counts.data[s.counts + sig.pops.len + i]::usize;
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret n;
}

# what `ins` leaves secret, applied to `p`: its writes take whether anything it reads is secret, but a register `moves`
# derives, which takes its inputs', in every row overlapping a register written, a row the write leaves part of keeping
# that part's old secret, and its stores hold the extent they write. a register written holds no known offset from the
# stack pointer after it but where `moves` gives one. a call, whose callee the walk does not read, leaves every register
# and every address secret when anything is, and no register of a known offset, unless `model` states its callee, as
# `modeled` applies with `joined` its join
fun apply(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: usize, ins: *walk.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint, value: bool, model: *Call, joined: bool) err[A.Error] {
    val version: u64          = at::u64 * 2 + 1;
    val moved:   err[A.Error] = moves(w, p, ins, fp);
    if (sel moved.err) { ret moved; }
    val formed: err[A.Error] = formings(w, p, ins);
    if (sel formed.err) { ret formed; }
    if (model != nil) {
        val saving: err[A.Error] = save_stack(w, p);
        if (sel saving.err) { ret saving; }
    }
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < w.file.register_count) {
        val written: bool = bit_of(fp.written.data, i) || bit_of(fp.clobbers.data, i);
        # a write through a register reading zero is discarded
        if (written && (w.file.registers[i].flags & register.ZERO) == 0) {
            val secret: bool                        = written_secret(w, i, value);
            val span:   res[register.Span, A.Error] = register.overlapping(?w.overlaps, i);
            if (sel span.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{span.err}; }
            var k: u32 = 0;
            for (k < span.ok.count) {
                val o:   u32                = w.overlaps.rows.data[span.ok.first + k];
                val row: *register.Register = ?w.file.registers[o];
                if (stored(w, o)) {
                    if (footprint.kills(fp, register.id_of(row))) { set_bit(p.taint.data, o, secret); }
                    or (secret)                                   { set_bit(p.taint.data, o, true); }
                    p.versions.data[o] = version;
                    p.frames.data[o]   = UNKNOWN;
                    p.formed.data[o]   = UNFORMED;
                }
                k = k + 1;
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    var m: usize = 0;
    for (m < w.moved.len) {
        p.frames.data[w.moved.data[m].row] = Frame{known: true, offset: w.moved.data[m].offset};
        m                                  = m + 1;
    }
    m = 0;
    for (m < w.forming.len) {
        p.formed.data[w.forming.data[m].row] = w.forming.data[m].formed;
        m                                    = m + 1;
    }
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < w.touches.len) {
        val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[k];
        if (t.writes && value) {
            unpublish(w, p, ?t.at);
            if (!located(?t.at)) { everywhere(p); }
            or {
                val held: err[A.Error] = hold(p, t.at);
                if (sel held.err) { ret held; }
            }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    if (fp.control.transfer == effect.CALL && model != nil) {
        val made: err[A.Error] = modeled(w, p, version, model, joined);
        if (sel made.err) { ret made; }
    }
    or (fp.control.transfer == effect.CALL) {
        var secret: bool  = memory_secret(w, p);
        var word:   usize = 0;
        for (word < w.words) {
            if (p.taint.data[word] != 0) { secret = true; }
            word = word + 1;
        }
        i = 0;
        for (i < w.file.register_count) {
            if (stored(w, i)) {
                if (secret) { set_bit(p.taint.data, i, true); }
                p.versions.data[i] = version;
                p.frames.data[i]   = UNKNOWN;
                p.formed.data[i]   = UNFORMED;
            }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        if (secret) {
            everywhere(p);
            keep_private(w, p);
        }
    }
    val hooks: *config.Hooks = w.code.set.config;
    if (hooks != nil) {
        val est: config.Established = hooks.establish(ins.inst.row, operand.Values{at: ins.inst.values, len: ins.inst.count});
        if (sel est.sets)      { p.config = opt[config.State].some{est.sets}; }
        if (sel est.undecided) { p.config = opt[config.State].none{}; }
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# the stack pointer's row and the rows lying within it, as they are under `p` where a call starts, into `w.saved`
fun save_stack(w: *Walk, p: *Point) err[A.Error] {
    vector.truncate[Saved](?w.saved, 0);
    if (w.stack == effect.NO_ROW) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
    val span: res[register.Span, A.Error] = register.overlapping(?w.overlaps, w.stack);
    if (sel span.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{span.err}; }
    val sp: *register.Register = ?w.file.registers[w.stack];
    var k:  u32                = 0;
    for (k <= span.ok.count) {
        var o: u32 = w.stack;
        if (k < span.ok.count) { o = w.overlaps.rows.data[span.ok.first + k]; }
        if (o == w.stack || register.overwrites(w.file, sp, ?w.file.registers[o], opt[register.Extend].some{register.KEEP})) {
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Saved](?w.saved, Saved{row: o, taint: bit_of(p.taint.data, o), version: p.versions.data[o], frame: p.frames.data[o]});
            if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# the rows of the registers `regs` names marked in `into`, cleared first: each row, and with `within` the rows lying
# within it, else every row sharing storage with it
fun mark_rows(w: *Walk, regs: *Registers, within: bool, into: *u64) err[A.Error] {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < w.words) {
        into[i] = 0;
        i       = i + 1;
    }
    var n: u32 = 0;
    for (n < regs.len) {
        val row: u32 = row_or_none(w, regs.at[n]);
        set_bit(into, row, true);
        val span: res[register.Span, A.Error] = register.overlapping(?w.overlaps, row);
        if (sel span.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{span.err}; }
        val by: *register.Register = ?w.file.registers[row];
        var k:  u32                = 0;
        for (k < span.ok.count) {
            val o: u32 = w.overlaps.rows.data[span.ok.first + k];
            if (!within || register.overwrites(w.file, by, ?w.file.registers[o], opt[register.Extend].some{register.KEEP})) { set_bit(into, o, true); }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        n = n + 1;
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# the extents `e` names placed under `p`, where a call starts, into `into`
fun place_extents(w: *Walk, p: *Point, e: *Extents, into: *vector.Vector[Held]) err[A.Error] {
    vector.truncate[Held](into, 0);
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < e.len) {
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](into, extent_held(w, p, ?e.at[i]));
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# extent `x` placed under `p`, where a call starts: off its base register's value, its symbol's address, or an absolute
# address the walk does not place
fun extent_held(w: *Walk, p: *Point, x: *Extent) Held {
    if (x.base != register.NONE) { ret rebase(w, p, row_or_none(w, x.base), x.offset, x.length); }
    ret Held{base: effect.NO_ROW, version: ENTRY, symbol: x.symbol, slot: false, offset: x.offset, length: x.length};
}

# whether every byte of `at` is one of an extent `w.kept` holds
fun in_kept(w: *Walk, at: *Held) bool {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < w.kept.len) {
        if (inside(at, ?w.kept.data[i])) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# the join of a call and what it accepts
# ---
# secret:     whether an argument register, an extent it reads, or any memory it does not keep, unless confined, may hold
#             a secret
# unaccepted: whether one of those the model does not state the callee accepts a secret in may: an argument register
#             or a read extent it does not accept, or memory it does not keep that no accepted read holds whole
rec Joined {
    secret:     bool;
    unaccepted: bool;
}

# whether model `c` accepts a secret in register `reg`
fun accepts(c: *Call, reg: register.Id) bool {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < c.accepted.len) {
        if (c.accepted.at[i] == reg) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether extents `x` and `y` are stated alike
fun same_extent(x: *Extent, y: *Extent) bool {
    ret x.base == y.base && x.symbol == y.symbol && x.offset == y.offset && x.length == y.length;
}

# whether model `c` accepts a secret in its read extent `x`
fun accepts_read(c: *Call, x: *Extent) bool {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < c.accepted_reads.len) {
        if (same_extent(?c.accepted_reads.at[i], x)) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether an extent model `c` accepts a secret in holds every byte of `h` under `r`, where the call starts
fun accepted_whole(w: *Walk, r: *Point, c: *Call, h: *Held) bool {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < c.accepted_reads.len) {
        val a: Held = extent_held(w, r, ?c.accepted_reads.at[i]);
        if (inside(h, ?a)) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# the join of the call modeled by `c` under `r`, where it starts, and whether a secret reaches it through what it does
# not accept, its kept and written extents placed into `w.kept` and `w.wrote`. a confined callee reads no memory it
# does not keep, so that memory joins nothing
fun join(w: *Walk, r: *Point, c: *Call) res[Joined, A.Error] {
    val placed_kept: err[A.Error] = place_extents(w, r, ?c.kept, ?w.kept);
    if (sel placed_kept.err) { ret failed[Joined](placed_kept.err); }
    val placed_wrote: err[A.Error] = place_extents(w, r, ?c.writes, ?w.wrote);
    if (sel placed_wrote.err) { ret failed[Joined](placed_wrote.err); }
    var j: Joined = Joined{secret: false, unaccepted: false};
    var i: u32    = 0;
    for (i < c.arguments.len) {
        if (tainted(w, r, c.arguments.at[i])) {
            j.secret = true;
            if (!accepts(c, c.arguments.at[i])) { j.unaccepted = true; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < c.reads.len) {
        val h: Held = extent_held(w, r, ?c.reads.at[i]);
        if (secret_at(w, r, ?h)) {
            j.secret = true;
            if (!accepts_read(c, ?c.reads.at[i])) { j.unaccepted = true; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    if (c.confined) { ret res[Joined, A.Error].ok{j}; }
    if (r.anywhere) {
        j.secret     = true;
        j.unaccepted = true;
    }
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < r.held.len) {
        if (!in_kept(w, ?r.held.data[k]) && !is_private(w, ?r.held.data[k])) {
            j.secret = true;
            if (!accepted_whole(w, r, c, ?r.held.data[k])) { j.unaccepted = true; }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret res[Joined, A.Error].ok{j};
}

# the call modeled by `c`, whose own instruction `apply` has applied to `p`, leaving its callee's effects at `version`:
# a preserved row and a program counter's, the return point, keep what the instruction left and the stack pointer's
# rows what `w.saved` holds, a written row takes `joined`, and a row it states neither is secret when anything is, as
# with no model, each of the others of the version and of no known offset. with `joined` every byte it does not keep
# may hold a secret, and every extent it writes does
fun modeled(w: *Walk, p: *Point, version: u64, c: *Call, joined: bool) err[A.Error] {
    val keeping: err[A.Error] = mark_rows(w, ?c.preserved, true, w.keeping.data);
    if (sel keeping.err) { ret keeping; }
    val writing: err[A.Error] = mark_rows(w, ?c.written, false, w.writing.data);
    if (sel writing.err) { ret writing; }
    var secret: bool  = memory_secret(w, p);
    var word:   usize = 0;
    for (word < w.words) {
        if (p.taint.data[word] != 0) { secret = true; }
        word = word + 1;
    }
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < w.file.register_count) {
        val pc: bool = (w.file.registers[i].flags & register.PC) != 0;
        if (stored(w, i) && !pc && !bit_of(w.keeping.data, i)) {
            if (bit_of(w.writing.data, i)) { set_bit(p.taint.data, i, joined); }
            or (secret)                    { set_bit(p.taint.data, i, true); }
            p.versions.data[i] = version;
            p.frames.data[i]   = UNKNOWN;
            p.formed.data[i]   = UNFORMED;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < w.saved.len) {
        val sv: *Saved = ?w.saved.data[k];
        set_bit(p.taint.data, sv.row, sv.taint);
        p.versions.data[sv.row] = sv.version;
        p.frames.data[sv.row]   = sv.frame;
        k                       = k + 1;
    }
    if (!joined) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
    var left: usize = 0;
    k = 0;
    for (k < p.public.len) {
        if (in_kept(w, ?p.public.data[k]) || is_private(w, ?p.public.data[k])) {
            p.public.data[left] = p.public.data[k];
            left                = left + 1;
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    vector.truncate[Held](?p.public, left);
    if (p.anywhere) {
        val narrowed: res[bool, A.Error] = narrow(w, ?p.spared, ?w.kept);
        if (sel narrowed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{narrowed.err}; }
    }
    or {
        p.anywhere = true;
        vector.truncate[Held](?p.spared, 0);
        k = 0;
        for (k < w.kept.len) {
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?p.spared, w.kept.data[k]);
            if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
    }
    k = 0;
    for (k < w.wrote.len) {
        val h: Held = w.wrote.data[k];
        unpublish(w, p, ?h);
        if (!located(?h)) { everywhere(p); }
        or {
            val held: err[A.Error] = hold(p, h);
            if (sel held.err) { ret held; }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

fun unread(message: str, at: usize) opt[Verdict] {
    ret opt[Verdict].some{Verdict.unread{Unread{message: message, offset: at::u64}}};
}

fun refused(r: ct.Refusal, at: usize) opt[Verdict] {
    ret opt[Verdict].some{Verdict.refused{Finding{offset: at::u64, refusal: r}}};
}

fun stays(at: usize) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNBALANCED, at)};
}

# `p` reaching `to` from the instruction at `at`, unread when control joins there at another height of the stack
fun goes(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: usize, to: usize) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    val reached: res[bool, A.Error] = reach(w, p, to);
    if (sel reached.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](reached.err); }
    if (!reached.ok)     { ret stays(at); }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

# where a branch to block `b` goes: a loop's start, else its close
fun label_of(b: *Block) usize {
    if (b.loops) { ret b.body; }
    ret b.close;
}

# the blocks the depths of the instruction of shape `s` at `at` name, each reached with `p` cut to its block's height
# and the values `w.carried` holds on top
fun branches(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: usize, s: *Shape) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < s.depths) {
        val b: *Block = ?w.blocks.data[w.targets.data[s.targets + i]];
        if (p.stack.len < b.base::usize) { ret stays(at); }
        val made: res[Point, A.Error] = copy(w, p);
        if (sel made.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](made.err); }
        var edge: Point = made.ok;
        vector.truncate[bool](?edge.stack, b.base::usize);
        var k: usize = 0;
        for (k < w.carried.len) {
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[bool](?edge.stack, w.carried.data[k]);
            if (sel pushed.err) {
                drop(?edge);
                ret failed[opt[Verdict]](pushed.err);
            }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        val went: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = goes(w, ?edge, at, label_of(b));
        drop(?edge);
        if (sel went.err)     { ret went; }
        if (sel went.ok.some) { ret went; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

# the instruction starts control reaches from `ins` at `at`, each reached with `p`: a typed stream's branch to the
# blocks its depths name or where the block it opens or splits goes on, a jump to its relative target but a modeled
# tail call, `tail`, whose path ends, and the next instruction unless it jumps, returns or faults unconditionally or
# leaves the stack polymorphic
# ---
# ret: none when every one is in the code, else why the walk cannot follow it
fun successors(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: usize, ins: *walk.Decoded, c: *effect.Control, s: *Shape, tail: bool) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    val next:  usize = at + ins.len;
    var falls: bool  = effect.falls(c);
    if (s != nil && s.stuck) { falls = false; }
    if (c.transfer == effect.JUMP && c.target == effect.DEPTH && s != nil) {
        val went: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = branches(w, p, at, s);
        if (sel went.err)     { ret went; }
        if (sel went.ok.some) { ret went; }
    }
    or (c.transfer == effect.JUMP && c.target == effect.STRUCTURED && s != nil && s.block != NO_BLOCK) {
        val b:  *Block = ?w.blocks.data[s.block];
        var to: usize  = b.close;
        if (effect.opens(ins.inst.row.effect.structure) && b.split != NO_OFFSET) { to = b.split + w.shapes.data[w.shaped.data[b.split]].len; }
        val went: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = goes(w, p, at, to);
        if (sel went.err)     { ret went; }
        if (sel went.ok.some) { ret went; }
    }
    or (c.transfer == effect.JUMP && !tail) {
        if (c.target != effect.DIRECT || c.operand == field.NO_OPERAND || c.operand::u32 >= ins.inst.count) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(INDIRECT, at)}; }
        val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[c.operand];
        if (!sel v.relative) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(NOWHERE, at)}; }
        var from:  i64           = at::i64;
        val shape: operand.Shape = ins.inst.row.operands.at[c.operand].shape;
        if (sel shape.relative && shape.relative.anchor == operand.END) { from = next::i64; }
        val to: i64 = from + v.relative;
        if (to < 0 || to >= w.code.len::i64)                  { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(NOWHERE, at)}; }
        if (s != nil && w.shaped.data[to::usize] == NO_POINT) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(NOWHERE, at)}; }
        val went: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = goes(w, p, at, to::usize);
        if (sel went.err)     { ret went; }
        if (sel went.ok.some) { ret went; }
    }
    if (falls && next < w.code.len) { ret goes(w, p, at, next); }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

# `h` added to the extents `p` knows public unless it knows it
fun publish(p: *Point, h: Held) err[A.Error] {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < p.public.len) {
        if (same(?p.public.data[i], ?h)) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?p.public, h);
    if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# the extent `e` of the memory a declassify point names as the touch of the instruction walked formed from its base
# register and holding it whole would name it, or off its symbol as a touch the sites place holding it whole names it,
# a touch that writes for `writes` and else one that reads. none when no touch does, or `e` is of no register row or
# symbol or of no length
fun held_by_touch(w: *Walk, e: *Extent, writes: bool) opt[Held] {
    if (e.symbol != operand.NO_SYMBOL && e.base == register.NONE && e.length != 0) {
        val g: Held  = Held{base: effect.NO_ROW, version: ENTRY, symbol: e.symbol, slot: false, offset: e.offset, length: e.length};
        var n: usize = 0;
        for (n < w.touches.len) {
            val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[n];
            if (((writes && t.writes) || (!writes && t.reads)) && inside(?g, ?t.at)) { ret opt[Held].some{g}; }
            n = n + 1;
        }
        ret opt[Held].none{};
    }
    val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, e.base);
    if (sel row.none)  { ret opt[Held].none{}; }
    if (e.length == 0) { ret opt[Held].none{}; }
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < w.touches.len) {
        val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[k];
        val h: Held   = Held{base: t.at.base, version: t.at.version, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: e.offset + t.rebased, length: e.length};
        if (t.row == row.some && ((writes && t.writes) || (!writes && t.reads)) && inside(?h, ?t.at)) { ret opt[Held].some{h}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret opt[Held].none{};
}

# the frame slot `e` a declassify point names, off its base register's value under `pre`, the state where the
# instruction walked starts, when a touch of that instruction holds it whole, one that writes for `writes` and else one
# that reads, through whichever register. none when no touch does, or `e` is of no register row or of no length
fun held_by_frame(w: *Walk, pre: *Point, e: *Extent, writes: bool) opt[Held] {
    val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, e.base);
    if (sel row.none)  { ret opt[Held].none{}; }
    if (e.length == 0) { ret opt[Held].none{}; }
    val h: Held  = rebase(w, pre, row.some, e.offset, e.length);
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < w.touches.len) {
        val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[k];
        if (((writes && t.writes) || (!writes && t.reads)) && inside(?h, ?t.at)) { ret opt[Held].some{h}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret opt[Held].none{};
}

# whether `ins` reads, for `role` operand.READ, or writes, for operand.WRITE, the entry of key `k` through an operand
# holding its id
fun names_entry(ins: *walk.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint, k: u64, role: operand.Role) bool {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < fp.entries.len) {
        val n: *effect.Entry = ?fp.entries.at[i];
        if ((n.role & role) != 0) {
            val got: opt[u64] = entry_key(ins, n.operand);
            if (sel got.some) {
                if (got.some == k) { ret true; }
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

fun touched(ok: bool) res[bool, A.Error] {
    ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{ok};
}

# register row `row` made public in `p`, and every row a write through it extending as `extend` overwrites, as
# `register.overwrites` decides: KEEP for the rows lying within it, or what the write a point after it names leaves
fun publish_row(w: *Walk, p: *Point, row: u32, extend: opt[register.Extend]) err[A.Error] {
    set_bit(p.taint.data, row, false);
    val span: res[register.Span, A.Error] = register.overlapping(?w.overlaps, row);
    if (sel span.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{span.err}; }
    val by: *register.Register = ?w.file.registers[row];
    var k:  u32                = 0;
    for (k < span.ok.count) {
        val o: u32 = w.overlaps.rows.data[span.ok.first + k];
        if (register.overwrites(w.file, by, ?w.file.registers[o], extend)) { set_bit(p.taint.data, o, false); }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# the place of the declassify point `d` before `ins` made public in `r`, the state the instruction's reads are decided
# under: a register row it reads, an entry it reads through an operand holding its id, a value it pops, and with
# `memory` set, once `w.touches` holds its touches, an extent one it reads holds whole. a place of the other pass is
# left as it is
# ---
# ret: whether the instruction reads the place, false refusing the point
fun lift(w: *Walk, r: *Point, ins: *walk.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint, s: *Shape, d: *Declassify, memory: bool) res[bool, A.Error] {
    val q: Place = d.place;
    if (sel q.memory) {
        if (!memory) { ret touched(true); }
        val h: opt[Held] = held_by_touch(w, ?q.memory, false);
        if (sel h.none) { ret touched(false); }
        val made: err[A.Error] = publish(r, h.some);
        if (sel made.err) { ret failed[bool](made.err); }
        ret touched(true);
    }
    if (sel q.frame) {
        if (!memory) { ret touched(true); }
        val h: opt[Held] = held_by_frame(w, r, ?q.frame, false);
        if (sel h.none) { ret touched(false); }
        val made: err[A.Error] = publish(r, h.some);
        if (sel made.err) { ret failed[bool](made.err); }
        ret touched(true);
    }
    if (memory) { ret touched(true); }
    if (sel q.register) {
        val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, q.register);
        if (sel row.none)                     { ret touched(false); }
        if (!bit_of(fp.reads.data, row.some)) { ret touched(false); }
        val made: err[A.Error] = publish_row(w, r, row.some, opt[register.Extend].some{register.KEEP});
        if (sel made.err) { ret failed[bool](made.err); }
        ret touched(true);
    }
    if (sel q.entry) {
        val k: u64 = key(q.entry.space, q.entry.index);
        if (!names_entry(ins, fp, k, operand.READ)) { ret touched(false); }
        val set: err[A.Error] = set_entry(r, k, false);
        if (sel set.err) { ret failed[bool](set.err); }
        ret touched(true);
    }
    if (sel q.value) {
        if (s == nil || q.value::usize >= pop_count(w, s, ?fp.signature)) { ret touched(false); }
        r.stack.data[r.stack.len - 1 - q.value::usize] = false;
        ret touched(true);
    }
    ret touched(false);
}

# the place of the declassify point `d` after `ins` made to hold no secret in `p`, the state the instruction leaves: a
# register row it writes, an entry it writes through an operand holding its id, a value of the `left` it leaves on top
# of the stack, and an extent one of its touches writes whole, known public until a secret may be stored there. a frame
# slot is placed off its base register under `pre`, the state where the instruction starts
# ---
# ret: whether the instruction writes the place, false refusing the point
fun clear(w: *Walk, p: *Point, pre: *Point, ins: *walk.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint, d: *Declassify, left: usize) res[bool, A.Error] {
    val q: Place = d.place;
    if (sel q.memory) {
        val h: opt[Held] = held_by_touch(w, ?q.memory, true);
        if (sel h.none) { ret touched(false); }
        val made: err[A.Error] = publish(p, h.some);
        if (sel made.err) { ret failed[bool](made.err); }
        ret touched(true);
    }
    if (sel q.frame) {
        val h: opt[Held] = held_by_frame(w, pre, ?q.frame, true);
        if (sel h.none) { ret touched(false); }
        val made: err[A.Error] = publish(p, h.some);
        if (sel made.err) { ret failed[bool](made.err); }
        ret touched(true);
    }
    if (sel q.register) {
        val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, q.register);
        if (sel row.none)                                                              { ret touched(false); }
        if (!bit_of(fp.written.data, row.some) && !bit_of(fp.clobbers.data, row.some)) { ret touched(false); }
        var extend: opt[register.Extend] = opt[register.Extend].some{register.KEEP};
        var i:      usize                = 0;
        for (i < fp.writes.len) {
            if (fp.writes.data[i].at == q.register) { extend = fp.writes.data[i].write.extend; }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        val made: err[A.Error] = publish_row(w, p, row.some, extend);
        if (sel made.err) { ret failed[bool](made.err); }
        ret touched(true);
    }
    if (sel q.entry) {
        val k: u64 = key(q.entry.space, q.entry.index);
        if (!names_entry(ins, fp, k, operand.WRITE)) { ret touched(false); }
        val set: err[A.Error] = set_entry(p, k, false);
        if (sel set.err) { ret failed[bool](set.err); }
        ret touched(true);
    }
    if (sel q.value) {
        if (q.value::usize >= left) { ret touched(false); }
        p.stack.data[p.stack.len - 1 - q.value::usize] = false;
        ret touched(true);
    }
    ret touched(false);
}

# the declassify points before `ins` at `at` applied to `r`, its places of one pass as `lift` takes them
# ---
# ret: none when every one names a place the instruction reads, else the refusal of the first that does not
fun lifts(w: *Walk, r: *Point, at: usize, ins: *walk.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint, s: *Shape, memory: bool) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    var i: u32 = w.declared.data[at];
    for (i != NO_POINT) {
        val d: *Declassify = ?w.public.at[i];
        if (sel d.side.before) {
            val ok: res[bool, A.Error] = lift(w, r, ins, fp, s, d, memory);
            if (sel ok.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](ok.err); }
            if (!ok.ok)     { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNTOUCHED, at)}; }
        }
        i = w.chain.data[i];
    }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

# the instruction at `at` walked from the state there. a declassify point before it makes its place public in a copy
# of that state its reads are decided under, and one after it clears its place in the state it leaves
# ---
# ret: a verdict when it ends the walk, none to go on
fun step(w: *Walk, at: usize, store: *vector.Vector[operand.Value], alts: *vector.Vector[requirement.Alternative], fp: *footprint.Footprint) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    val held: res[Point, A.Error] = copy(w, ?w.states.data[w.points.data[at]]);
    if (sel held.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](held.err); }
    var p: Point = held.ok;
    fin { drop(?p); }
    val sowed: err[A.Error] = sow(w, ?p, at);
    if (sel sowed.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](sowed.err); }
    val got: res[walk.Decoded, field.Refusal] = walk.decode_grown(w.code.set.codec, w.ctx, w.code.data, w.code.len, at, store, alts);
    if (sel got.err) {
        if (sel got.err.cause.memory) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](got.err.cause.memory); }
        ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNDECODED, at)};
    }
    var ins: walk.Decoded = got.ok;
    w.at = at;
    val cfg:    config.Configured                                 = config.Configured{hooks: w.code.set.config, state: p.config};
    val values: operand.Values                                    = operand.Values{at: ins.inst.values, len: ins.inst.count};
    val foot:   res[effect.Answer[*footprint.Footprint], A.Error] = footprint.of(fp, ins.inst.row, values, w.ctx, cfg);
    if (sel foot.err)          { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](foot.err); }
    if (sel foot.ok.undecided) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNDECIDED, at)}; }
    var k: usize = at + 1;
    for (k < at + ins.len && k < w.code.len) {
        if (w.declared.data[k] != NO_POINT) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(MISPLACED, k)}; }
        if (w.called.data[k] != NO_POINT)   { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNCALLED, k)}; }
        if (w.sited.data[k] != NO_POINT)    { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSITED, k)}; }
        if (w.stated.data[k] != NO_POINT)   { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNACCESSED, k)}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    var n: u32 = w.sited.data[at];
    for (n != NO_POINT && n < w.code.sites.len && w.code.sites.at[n].at == at::u64) {
        if (w.code.sites.at[n].operand::u32 >= ins.inst.count) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSITED, at)}; }
        n = n + 1;
    }
    var model: *Call = nil;
    var tail:  bool  = false;
    if (w.called.data[at] != NO_POINT) {
        model = ?w.calls.at[w.called.data[at]];
        tail  = fp.control.transfer == effect.JUMP;
        if (fp.control.transfer != effect.CALL && !tail) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNCALLED, at)}; }
    }
    var shape:  *Shape = nil;
    var popped: usize  = 0;
    if (w.stream != nil) {
        shape  = ?w.shapes.data[w.shaped.data[at]];
        popped = pop_count(w, shape, ?fp.signature);
        if (p.stack.len < popped) { ret stays(at); }
    }
    var before: bool = false;
    var i:      u32  = w.declared.data[at];
    for (i != NO_POINT) {
        if (sel w.public.at[i].side.before) { before = true; }
        i = w.chain.data[i];
    }
    var lifted: Point;
    var r:      *Point = ?p;
    if (before) {
        val made: res[Point, A.Error] = copy(w, ?p);
        if (sel made.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](made.err); }
        lifted = made.ok;
        r      = ?lifted;
    }
    fin {
        if (before) { drop(?lifted); }
    }
    if (before) {
        val lifting: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = lifts(w, r, at, ?ins, fp, shape, false);
        if (sel lifting.err)     { ret lifting; }
        if (sel lifting.ok.some) { ret lifting; }
    }
    var stacked: bool = false;
    k = r.stack.len - popped;
    for (k < r.stack.len) {
        if (r.stack.data[k]) { stacked = true; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    k = 0;
    for (k < w.words) {
        w.named.data[k] = 0;
        k               = k + 1;
    }
    var secret: u32 = 0;
    var op:     u32 = 0;
    for (op < ins.inst.count) {
        if (operand_secret(w, r, ?ins, op::u8, cfg, w.named.data) && op < 32) { secret = secret | (1::u32 << op); }
        op = op + 1;
    }
    val address: res[opt[ct.Refusal], A.Error] = touches(w, r, ?ins, fp);
    if (sel address.err)     { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](address.err); }
    if (sel address.ok.some) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{refused(address.ok.some, at)}; }
    if (!accessed(w))        { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNACCESSED, at)}; }
    if (before) {
        val lifting: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = lifts(w, r, at, ?ins, fp, shape, true);
        if (sel lifting.err)     { ret lifting; }
        if (sel lifting.ok.some) { ret lifting; }
    }
    var read: bool = entries_read(r, ?ins, fp);
    k = 0;
    for (k < w.words) {
        if ((fp.reads.data[k] & r.taint.data[k]) != 0) { read = true; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    k = 0;
    for (k < w.touches.len) {
        if (reads_secret(w, r, ?w.touches.data[k])) { read = true; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    var c:        effect.Control  = fp.control;
    val transfer: opt[ct.Refusal] = control(w, r, ?ins, ?c, read, stacked, secret);
    if (sel transfer.some) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{refused(transfer.some, at)}; }
    if (w.timed) {
        val timing: opt[ct.Refusal] = latency(w, r, ?ins, fp, secret);
        if (sel timing.some) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{refused(timing.some, at)}; }
    }
    var joined: bool = false;
    if (model != nil) {
        val j: res[Joined, A.Error] = join(w, r, model);
        if (sel j.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](j.err); }
        joined = j.ok.secret;
        if (j.ok.unaccepted) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{refused(ct.refusal(ct.UNCHECKED, field.NO_OPERAND), at)}; }
        if (tail)            { model = nil; }
    }
    val value: bool = read || stacked;
    if (value) {
        k = 0;
        for (k < w.touches.len) {
            val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[k];
            if (t.writes && t.seeded && !t.secret) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{refused(ct.refusal(ct.STORED, first_secret(secret, ins.inst.count)), at)}; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
    }
    if (shape != nil && c.target == effect.DEPTH) {
        val kept: err[A.Error] = carry(w, ?p, shape, ?fp.signature, effect.TypeRef.operand{c.operand});
        if (sel kept.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](kept.err); }
    }
    val applied: err[A.Error] = apply(w, ?p, at, ?ins, fp, value, model, joined);
    if (sel applied.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](applied.err); }
    val bottom: usize = p.stack.len - popped;
    if (shape != nil) {
        val streamed: err[A.Error] = apply_stream(w, ?p, ?ins, fp, shape, value);
        if (sel streamed.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](streamed.err); }
    }
    i = w.declared.data[at];
    for (i != NO_POINT) {
        val d: *Declassify = ?w.public.at[i];
        if (sel d.side.after) {
            val ok: res[bool, A.Error] = clear(w, ?p, ?w.states.data[w.points.data[at]], ?ins, fp, d, p.stack.len - bottom);
            if (sel ok.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](ok.err); }
            if (!ok.ok)     { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNTOUCHED, at)}; }
        }
        i = w.chain.data[i];
    }
    ret successors(w, ?p, at, ?ins, ?c, shape, tail);
}

# the entry state the seeds make, a register's secret in every row overlapping it but one reading zero, a global's off
# its symbol, the frame seeds indexed by offset into `w.sown` and `w.sowing`, and the access seeds into `w.stated` and
# `w.sowing`, refused naming a register the file has no row of, an entry the stream does not hold, a frame slot or an
# access at one past the code, memory or a slot off a symbol, or a global of no symbol
fun seed(w: *Walk, secrets: *Secrets, p: *Point) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < secrets.len) {
        val s: Seed = secrets.at[i];
        if (sel s.register) {
            val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, s.register);
            if (sel row.none) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            val span: res[register.Span, A.Error] = register.overlapping(?w.overlaps, row.some);
            if (sel span.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](span.err); }
            var k: u32 = 0;
            for (k < span.ok.count) {
                val o: u32 = w.overlaps.rows.data[span.ok.first + k];
                if (stored(w, o)) { set_bit(p.taint.data, o, true); }
                k = k + 1;
            }
        }
        if (sel s.memory) {
            if (s.memory.symbol != operand.NO_SYMBOL) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            var h: Held = Held{base: effect.NO_ROW, version: ENTRY, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: s.memory.offset, length: s.memory.length};
            if (s.memory.base != register.NONE) {
                val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, s.memory.base);
                if (sel row.none) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
                h = rebase(w, p, row.some, s.memory.offset, s.memory.length);
            }
            val held: err[A.Error] = hold(p, h);
            if (sel held.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](held.err); }
        }
        if (sel s.symbol) {
            if (s.symbol.symbol == operand.NO_SYMBOL) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            val held: err[A.Error] = hold(p, Held{base: effect.NO_ROW, version: ENTRY, symbol: s.symbol.symbol, slot: false, offset: s.symbol.offset, length: s.symbol.length});
            if (sel held.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](held.err); }
        }
        if (sel s.private) {
            if (w.stack == effect.NO_ROW || w.stream != nil || s.private.length == 0) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?w.private, Held{base: w.stack, version: ENTRY, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: s.private.offset, length: s.private.length});
            if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](pushed.err); }
        }
        var next: u32 = NO_POINT;
        if (sel s.frame) {
            if (s.frame.extent.symbol != operand.NO_SYMBOL) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, s.frame.extent.base);
            if (sel row.none)                  { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            if (s.frame.at >= w.code.len::u64) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, s.frame.at::usize)}; }
            next                           = w.sown.data[s.frame.at::usize];
            w.sown.data[s.frame.at::usize] = i;
        }
        if (sel s.access) {
            if (s.access.at >= w.code.len::u64) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, s.access.at::usize)}; }
            next                              = w.stated.data[s.access.at::usize];
            w.stated.data[s.access.at::usize] = i;
        }
        val chained: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.sowing, next);
        if (sel chained.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](chained.err); }
        if (sel s.entry) {
            if (w.stream == nil) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            val there: opt[u32] = w.stream.space(w.ctx.stream, s.entry.space, s.entry.index);
            if (sel there.none) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            val set: err[A.Error] = set_entry(p, key(s.entry.space, s.entry.index), true);
            if (sel set.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](set.err); }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

# the frame seeds at `at` held in `p`, the state where the instruction there starts, each slot off its base register's
# value under it
fun sow(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: usize) err[A.Error] {
    var i: u32 = w.sown.data[at];
    for (i != NO_POINT) {
        val sd: Seed = w.secrets.at[i];
        if (sel sd.frame) {
            val e:   Extent   = sd.frame.extent;
            val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, e.base);
            if (sel row.some) {
                val held: err[A.Error] = hold(p, rebase(w, p, row.some, e.offset, e.length));
                if (sel held.err) { ret held; }
            }
        }
        i = w.sowing.data[i];
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# the height `height` of the operand stack less `n` values, none when that passes below `base`, its block's, and
# `base` in code no control reaches past a polymorphic stack, whose pops take values that are never there
fun lowered(height: u32, n: u32, base: u32, dead: bool) opt[u32] {
    if (height >= base + n) { ret opt[u32].some{height - n}; }
    if (dead)               { ret opt[u32].some{base}; }
    ret opt[u32].none{};
}

# whether every popped value the effect `e` and the control `c` name by depth is one of the `popped` an instruction pops
fun names_popped(e: *effect.Effect, c: *effect.Control, popped: u32) bool {
    if (c.condition::u32 > popped || c.chooses::u32 > popped) { ret false; }
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < e.memory.len) {
        val a: *effect.Access = ?e.memory.at[i];
        if (a.pop::u32 > popped) { ret false; }
        val count: effect.Count = a.width.count;
        if (sel count.popped) {
            if (count.popped::u32 >= popped) { ret false; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret true;
}

# the counts of each type of signature `sig` of `ins` pushed onto `w.counts`, its pops' then its pushes', as the
# stream resolves each, 0 for the polymorphic stack
# ---
# ret: how many values it pops and pushes, none for a type the stream does not resolve
rec Counted {
    pops:   u32;
    pushes: u32;
}

fun counted(w: *Walk, ins: *walk.Decoded, sig: *effect.Signature) res[opt[Counted], A.Error] {
    var c: Counted = Counted{pops: 0, pushes: 0};
    var i: u32     = 0;
    for (i < sig.pops.len + sig.pushes.len) {
        var ref:    effect.TypeRef = effect.TypeRef.polymorphic{};
        var pushed: bool           = i >= sig.pops.len;
        if (pushed) { ref = sig.pushes.at[i - sig.pops.len]; }
        or          { ref = sig.pops.at[i]; }
        var n: u32 = 0;
        if (!sel ref.polymorphic) {
            val got: opt[u32] = w.stream.arity(w.ctx.stream, ?ins.inst, ref, pushed);
            if (sel got.none) { ret res[opt[Counted], A.Error].ok{opt[Counted].none{}}; }
            n = got.some;
        }
        val kept: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.counts, n);
        if (sel kept.err) { ret failed[opt[Counted]](kept.err); }
        if (pushed)       { c.pushes = c.pushes + n; }
        or                { c.pops = c.pops + n; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[opt[Counted], A.Error].ok{opt[Counted].some{c}};
}

# the blocks the depths of control `c` of `ins` name added to `w.targets`, by the blocks `open` holds open, innermost
# last
# ---
# ret: how many, none for a depth past every block open or an operand holding no depth
fun depths(w: *Walk, ins: *walk.Decoded, c: *effect.Control, open: *vector.Vector[u32]) res[opt[u32], A.Error] {
    if (c.target != effect.DEPTH)                                          { ret res[opt[u32], A.Error].ok{opt[u32].some{0}}; }
    if (c.operand == field.NO_OPERAND || c.operand::u32 >= ins.inst.count) { ret res[opt[u32], A.Error].ok{opt[u32].none{}}; }
    val v:    operand.Value  = ins.inst.values[c.operand];
    var one:  [1]operand.Value;
    var list: operand.Values = operand.Values{at: ?one[0], len: 1};
    one[0] = v;
    if (sel v.list) { list = v.list; }
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < list.len) {
        val d: operand.Value = list.at[i];
        if (!sel d.id)               { ret res[opt[u32], A.Error].ok{opt[u32].none{}}; }
        if (d.id::usize >= open.len) { ret res[opt[u32], A.Error].ok{opt[u32].none{}}; }
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.targets, open.data[open.len - 1 - d.id::usize]);
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[opt[u32]](pushed.err); }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[opt[u32], A.Error].ok{opt[u32].some{list.len}};
}

# how many values of the pops of signature `sig`, whose counts start at `first` in `w.counts`, a block takes as its
# params: those of each type the instruction opening it pushes again
fun params_of(w: *Walk, sig: *effect.Signature, first: u32) u32 {
    var n: u32 = 0;
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < sig.pops.len) {
        if (pushed_again(sig, sig.pops.at[i])) { n = n + w.counts.data[first + i]; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret n;
}

# the code of a typed stream read once in its own order, each instruction observed on the context's stream after it is
# read: how many values each type of its signature stands for, the blocks it opens, splits and closes, matched by
# their structure, the height of the operand stack below each block's params, and the blocks its depths name
# ---
# ret: none when every instruction reads and every block opened closes in order, else why the code cannot be followed
fun scan(w: *Walk, store: *vector.Vector[operand.Value], alts: *vector.Vector[requirement.Alternative]) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    var open: vector.Vector[u32] = vector.init[u32](w.a);
    fin { vector.dnit[u32](?open); }
    val root: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Block](?w.blocks, Block{open: NO_OFFSET, body: 0, split: NO_OFFSET, close: NO_OFFSET, base: 0, params: 0, results: 0, loops: false});
    if (sel root.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](root.err); }
    val outer: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?open, 0);
    if (sel outer.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](outer.err); }
    var height: u32   = 0;
    var dead:   bool  = false;
    var at:     usize = 0;
    for (at < w.code.len) {
        if (open.len == 0) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSTRUCTURED, at)}; }
        val got: res[walk.Decoded, field.Refusal] = walk.decode_grown(w.code.set.codec, w.ctx, w.code.data, w.code.len, at, store, alts);
        if (sel got.err) {
            if (sel got.err.cause.memory) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](got.err.cause.memory); }
            ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNDECODED, at)};
        }
        var ins:    walk.Decoded                  = got.ok;
        val e:      *effect.Effect                = ins.inst.row.effect;
        val values: operand.Values                = operand.Values{at: ins.inst.values, len: ins.inst.count};
        val ctl:    effect.Answer[effect.Control] = effect.control(w.file, ins.inst.row.operands.at, e, values);
        if (sel ctl.undecided)             { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNDECIDED, at)}; }
        if (e.structure == effect.CATCHES) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(CAUGHT, at)}; }
        var c:     effect.Control             = ctl.decided;
        var shape: Shape                      = Shape{len: ins.len, counts: w.counts.len::u32, targets: w.targets.len::u32, depths: 0, block: NO_BLOCK, stuck: false};
        val sized: res[opt[Counted], A.Error] = counted(w, ?ins, ?e.signature);
        if (sel sized.err)     { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](sized.err); }
        if (sel sized.ok.none) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNTYPED, at)}; }
        val n: Counted = sized.ok.some;
        if (!names_popped(e, ?c, n.pops)) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNBALANCED, at)}; }
        var i: u32 = 0;
        for (i < e.signature.pushes.len) {
            if (sel e.signature.pushes.at[i].polymorphic) { shape.stuck = true; }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        val named: res[opt[u32], A.Error] = depths(w, ?ins, ?c, ?open);
        if (sel named.err)     { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](named.err); }
        if (sel named.ok.none) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSTRUCTURED, at)}; }
        shape.depths = named.ok.some;
        val top: u32              = open.data[open.len - 1];
        val s:   effect.Structure = e.structure;
        if (effect.opens(s)) {
            val params: u32      = params_of(w, ?e.signature, shape.counts);
            val below:  opt[u32] = lowered(height, n.pops, w.blocks.data[top].base, dead);
            if (sel below.none) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNBALANCED, at)}; }
            shape.block = w.blocks.len::u32;
            val opened: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Block](?w.blocks, Block{open: at, body: at + ins.len, split: NO_OFFSET, close: NO_OFFSET, base: below.some, params: params, results: n.pushes, loops: s == effect.LOOPS});
            if (sel opened.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](opened.err); }
            val nested: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?open, shape.block);
            if (sel nested.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](nested.err); }
            height = below.some + params;
            dead   = false;
        }
        or (s == effect.SPLITS) {
            val b: *Block = ?w.blocks.data[top];
            if (b.open == NO_OFFSET || b.loops || b.split != NO_OFFSET) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSTRUCTURED, at)}; }
            b.split     = at;
            shape.block = top;
            height      = b.base + b.params;
            dead        = false;
        }
        or (s == effect.CLOSES) {
            val b: *Block = ?w.blocks.data[top];
            b.close     = at;
            shape.block = top;
            vector.truncate[u32](?open, open.len - 1);
            height = b.base + b.results;
            dead   = false;
        }
        or {
            val below: opt[u32] = lowered(height, n.pops, w.blocks.data[top].base, dead);
            if (sel below.none) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNBALANCED, at)}; }
            height = below.some + n.pushes;
            if (shape.stuck) {
                height = w.blocks.data[top].base;
                dead   = true;
            }
        }
        w.shaped.data[at] = w.shapes.len::u32;
        val kept: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Shape](?w.shapes, shape);
        if (sel kept.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](kept.err); }
        val seen: err[field.Refusal] = w.stream.observe(w.ctx.stream, ?ins.inst);
        if (sel seen.err) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(seen.err.message, at)}; }
        at = at + ins.len;
    }
    if (open.len != 0) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSTRUCTURED, at)}; }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

fun release(w: *Walk) {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < w.states.len) {
        drop(?w.states.data[i]);
        i = i + 1;
    }
    vector.dnit[Point](?w.states);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.points);
    vector.dnit[usize](?w.work);
    vector.dnit[u64](?w.named);
    vector.dnit[Touch](?w.touches);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.shaped);
    vector.dnit[Shape](?w.shapes);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.counts);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.targets);
    vector.dnit[Block](?w.blocks);
    vector.dnit[bool](?w.carried);
    vector.dnit[bool](?w.popped);
    register.release_overlaps(?w.overlaps);
    vector.dnit[Moved](?w.moved);
    vector.dnit[Derived](?w.derived);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.sown);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.sowing);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.stated);
    vector.dnit[Held](?w.private);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.declared);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.chain);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.called);
    vector.dnit[u64](?w.keeping);
    vector.dnit[u64](?w.writing);
    vector.dnit[Held](?w.kept);
    vector.dnit[Held](?w.wrote);
    vector.dnit[Saved](?w.saved);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.sited);
    vector.dnit[Forming](?w.forming);
}

# the declassify points indexed by offset into `w.declared` and `w.chain`, refused at one past the code
fun index_points(w: *Walk) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < w.public.len) {
        val at: u64 = w.public.at[i].at;
        if (at >= w.code.len::u64) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(MISPLACED, at::usize)}; }
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.chain, w.declared.data[at::usize]);
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](pushed.err); }
        w.declared.data[at::usize] = i;
        i                          = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

# whether every register `regs` names has a row of the file
fun rowed(w: *Walk, regs: *Registers) bool {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < regs.len) {
        val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, regs.at[i]);
        if (sel row.none) { ret false; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret true;
}

# whether every extent `e` names is off no register or one with a row of the file, and none off both a register and a
# symbol
fun based(w: *Walk, e: *Extents) bool {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < e.len) {
        if (e.at[i].base != register.NONE && e.at[i].symbol != operand.NO_SYMBOL) { ret false; }
        if (e.at[i].base != register.NONE) {
            val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, e.at[i].base);
            if (sel row.none) { ret false; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret true;
}

# whether rows `x` and `y` share storage
fun shares(w: *Walk, x: u32, y: u32) res[bool, A.Error] {
    val span: res[register.Span, A.Error] = register.overlapping(?w.overlaps, x);
    if (sel span.err) { ret failed[bool](span.err); }
    var k: u32 = 0;
    for (k < span.ok.count) {
        if (w.overlaps.rows.data[span.ok.first + k] == y) { ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{true}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{x == y};
}

# the row of register `reg`, effect.NO_ROW for none
fun row_or_none(w: *Walk, reg: register.Id) u32 {
    val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, reg);
    if (sel row.some) { ret row.some; }
    ret effect.NO_ROW;
}

fun naming(message: str) res[opt[str], A.Error] {
    ret res[opt[str], A.Error].ok{opt[str].some{message}};
}

# the refusal of call model `c` by what it names alone, none when it may model a call: a register of no row, an extent
# off both a register and a symbol, a written register reading zero or sharing storage with a preserved one, an
# accepted register or read it does not name an argument or a read, and a preserved set without the stack pointer
fun malformed(w: *Walk, c: *Call) res[opt[str], A.Error] {
    if (!rowed(w, ?c.preserved) || !rowed(w, ?c.arguments) || !rowed(w, ?c.written)) { ret naming(UNWRITTEN); }
    if (!based(w, ?c.reads) || !based(w, ?c.writes) || !based(w, ?c.kept))           { ret naming(UNWRITTEN); }
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < c.accepted.len) {
        var named: bool = false;
        var k:     u32  = 0;
        for (k < c.arguments.len) {
            if (c.arguments.at[k] == c.accepted.at[i]) { named = true; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        if (!named) { ret naming(UNACCEPTED); }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < c.accepted_reads.len) {
        var named: bool = false;
        var k:     u32  = 0;
        for (k < c.reads.len) {
            if (same_extent(?c.reads.at[k], ?c.accepted_reads.at[i])) { named = true; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        if (!named) { ret naming(UNACCEPTED); }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < c.written.len) {
        val row: u32 = row_or_none(w, c.written.at[i]);
        if ((w.file.registers[row].flags & register.ZERO) != 0) { ret naming(UNWRITTEN); }
        var k: u32 = 0;
        for (k < c.preserved.len) {
            val both: res[bool, A.Error] = shares(w, row, row_or_none(w, c.preserved.at[k]));
            if (sel both.err) { ret failed[opt[str]](both.err); }
            if (both.ok)      { ret naming(UNWRITTEN); }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    if (w.stack == effect.NO_ROW) { ret res[opt[str], A.Error].ok{opt[str].none{}}; }
    i = 0;
    for (i < c.preserved.len) {
        if (row_or_none(w, c.preserved.at[i]) == w.stack) { ret res[opt[str], A.Error].ok{opt[str].none{}}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret naming(UNANCHORED);
}

# the call models indexed by offset into `w.called`, refused in code of a typed stream, at one past the code, as a
# second at an offset, or by what one names alone
fun index_calls(w: *Walk) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < w.calls.len) {
        val c:  *Call = ?w.calls.at[i];
        val at: u64   = c.at;
        if (w.stream != nil || at >= w.code.len::u64) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNCALLED, at::usize)}; }
        if (w.called.data[at::usize] != NO_POINT)     { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNCALLED, at::usize)}; }
        val bad: res[opt[str], A.Error] = malformed(w, c);
        if (sel bad.err)     { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](bad.err); }
        if (sel bad.ok.some) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(bad.ok.some, at::usize)}; }
        w.called.data[at::usize] = i;
        i                        = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

# the sites indexed by offset into `w.sited`, refused out of ascending order or at one past the code
fun index_sites(w: *Walk) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < w.code.sites.len) {
        val at: u64 = w.code.sites.at[i].at;
        if (at >= w.code.len::u64)                   { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSITED, at::usize)}; }
        if (i > 0 && w.code.sites.at[i - 1].at > at) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSITED, at::usize)}; }
        if (w.sited.data[at::usize] == NO_POINT)     { w.sited.data[at::usize] = i; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

fun walked(w: *Walk, secrets: *Secrets) res[Verdict, A.Error] {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < w.code.len) {
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.points, NO_POINT);
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[Verdict](pushed.err); }
        val declared: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.declared, NO_POINT);
        if (sel declared.err) { ret failed[Verdict](declared.err); }
        val sown: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.sown, NO_POINT);
        if (sel sown.err) { ret failed[Verdict](sown.err); }
        val stated: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.stated, NO_POINT);
        if (sel stated.err) { ret failed[Verdict](stated.err); }
        val called: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.called, NO_POINT);
        if (sel called.err) { ret failed[Verdict](called.err); }
        val sited: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.sited, NO_POINT);
        if (sel sited.err) { ret failed[Verdict](sited.err); }
        if (w.stream != nil) {
            val shaped: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.shaped, NO_POINT);
            if (sel shaped.err) { ret failed[Verdict](shaped.err); }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < w.words) {
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](?w.named, 0);
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[Verdict](pushed.err); }
        val keeping: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](?w.keeping, 0);
        if (sel keeping.err) { ret failed[Verdict](keeping.err); }
        val writing: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](?w.writing, 0);
        if (sel writing.err) { ret failed[Verdict](writing.err); }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    var store: vector.Vector[operand.Value] = vector.init[operand.Value](w.a);
    fin { vector.dnit[operand.Value](?store); }
    var alts: vector.Vector[requirement.Alternative] = vector.init[requirement.Alternative](w.a);
    fin { vector.dnit[requirement.Alternative](?alts); }
    val made: res[Point, A.Error] = blank(w);
    if (sel made.err) { ret failed[Verdict](made.err); }
    var entry: Point = made.ok;
    fin { drop(?entry); }
    val seeded: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = seed(w, secrets, ?entry);
    if (sel seeded.err)     { ret failed[Verdict](seeded.err); }
    if (sel seeded.ok.some) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{seeded.ok.some}; }
    val indexed: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = index_points(w);
    if (sel indexed.err)     { ret failed[Verdict](indexed.err); }
    if (sel indexed.ok.some) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{indexed.ok.some}; }
    val models: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = index_calls(w);
    if (sel models.err)     { ret failed[Verdict](models.err); }
    if (sel models.ok.some) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{models.ok.some}; }
    val sites: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = index_sites(w);
    if (sel sites.err)     { ret failed[Verdict](sites.err); }
    if (sel sites.ok.some) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{sites.ok.some}; }
    if (w.code.len == 0)   { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{Verdict.clear{}}; }
    if (w.stream != nil) {
        val read: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = scan(w, ?store, ?alts);
        if (sel read.err)     { ret failed[Verdict](read.err); }
        if (sel read.ok.some) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{read.ok.some}; }
    }
    val reached: res[bool, A.Error] = reach(w, ?entry, 0);
    if (sel reached.err) { ret failed[Verdict](reached.err); }
    val made_fp: res[footprint.Footprint, A.Error] = footprint.make(w.a, w.file);
    if (sel made_fp.err) { ret failed[Verdict](made_fp.err); }
    var fp: footprint.Footprint = made_fp.ok;
    fin { footprint.release(?fp); }
    for {
        val next: opt[usize] = vector.pop[usize](?w.work);
        if (sel next.none) { brk; }
        val stepped: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = step(w, next.some, ?store, ?alts, ?fp);
        if (sel stepped.err)     { ret failed[Verdict](stepped.err); }
        if (sel stepped.ok.some) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{stepped.ok.some}; }
    }
    # a point in code the walk never reaches, or within an instruction of code no path walks, is applied nowhere
    var n: u32 = 0;
    for (n < w.public.len) {
        val at: u64 = w.public.at[n].at;
        if (w.points.data[at::usize] == NO_POINT) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{Verdict.unread{Unread{message: MISPLACED, offset: at}}}; }
        n = n + 1;
    }
    # a call model at an offset no path reaches models nothing
    n = 0;
    for (n < w.calls.len) {
        val at: u64 = w.calls.at[n].at;
        if (w.points.data[at::usize] == NO_POINT) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{Verdict.unread{Unread{message: UNCALLED, offset: at}}}; }
        n = n + 1;
    }
    # a frame seed whose instruction no path reaches holds nowhere
    n = 0;
    for (n < secrets.len) {
        val s: Seed = secrets.at[n];
        if (sel s.frame) {
            if (w.points.data[s.frame.at::usize] == NO_POINT) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{Verdict.unread{Unread{message: UNSEEDABLE, offset: s.frame.at}}}; }
        }
        n = n + 1;
    }
    ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{Verdict.clear{}};
}

# the constant-time walk of `code` under the context the function runs under, from the secrets the caller seeds,
# public again only at the declassify points `public` states, NO_DECLASSIFIED for none, and each call walked through
# the model `calls` states at its offset, NO_CALLS for none, the conservative rule standing where none does. a
# set whose timing is `none` is refused before any walk, worded UNCLASSIFIED, and one whose timing is not guaranteed
# is walked asking no row's latency, code it clears answered unguaranteed. code of a typed stream is read once in its
# own order first, observed on the context's stream, which it leaves as reading the function's body leaves it, and is
# answered unread when its set classifies its rows' timing, as no class states inputs among the values a row pops
# ---
# ret: the verdict, or the allocator's refusal of the walk's storage
pub fun check(a: *A.Allocator, code: *Code, ctx: *state.Context, secrets: *Secrets, public: *Declassified, calls: *Calls) res[Verdict, A.Error] {
    val answer: ct.Required = ct.required(code.set.ct);
    if (sel answer.refused)                              { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{Verdict.refused{Finding{offset: 0, refusal: answer.refused}}}; }
    if (code.set.codec.stream != nil && sel answer.held) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{Verdict.unread{Unread{message: TIMED, offset: 0}}}; }
    var file: *register.File = code.set.codec.registers;
    if (file == nil) { file = ?NO_FILE; }
    val overlaps: res[register.Overlaps, A.Error] = register.overlaps_of(a, file);
    if (sel overlaps.err) { ret failed[Verdict](overlaps.err); }
    var w: Walk = Walk{
        a:        a,
        code:     code,
        timed:    sel answer.held,
        ctx:      ctx,
        file:     file,
        words:    effect.words(file)::usize,
        stream:   code.set.codec.stream,
        points:   vector.init[u32](a),
        states:   vector.init[Point](a),
        work:     vector.init[usize](a),
        named:    vector.init[u64](a),
        touches:  vector.init[Touch](a),
        shaped:   vector.init[u32](a),
        shapes:   vector.init[Shape](a),
        counts:   vector.init[u32](a),
        targets:  vector.init[u32](a),
        blocks:   vector.init[Block](a),
        carried:  vector.init[bool](a),
        popped:   vector.init[bool](a),
        public:   public,
        declared: vector.init[u32](a),
        chain:    vector.init[u32](a),
        overlaps: overlaps.ok,
        stack:    stack_row(file, code, ctx),
        moved:    vector.init[Moved](a),
        derived:  vector.init[Derived](a),
        secrets:  secrets,
        sown:     vector.init[u32](a),
        sowing:   vector.init[u32](a),
        stated:   vector.init[u32](a),
        private:  vector.init[Held](a),
        calls:    calls,
        called:   vector.init[u32](a),
        keeping:  vector.init[u64](a),
        writing:  vector.init[u64](a),
        kept:     vector.init[Held](a),
        wrote:    vector.init[Held](a),
        saved:    vector.init[Saved](a),
        arch:     arch_of(code, ctx),
        sited:    vector.init[u32](a),
        forming:  vector.init[Forming](a),
        at:       0,
    };
    val verdict: res[Verdict, A.Error] = walked(?w, secrets);
    release(?w);
    if (sel verdict.ok) {
        if (!w.timed && sel verdict.ok.clear) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{Verdict.unguaranteed{}}; }
    }
    ret verdict;
}
